WEBVTT

1
00:00:57.992 --> 00:01:00.959
   (Bee Gees's Staying Alive)

2
00:01:08.102 --> 00:01:10.169
      (indistinct chatter)

3
00:01:27.555 --> 00:01:29.421
           (laughter)

4
00:01:39.366 --> 00:01:41.433
      (background chatter)

5
00:01:53.147 --> 00:01:55.647
    - Come on, let's go out!

6
00:01:58.953 --> 00:02:00.986
         - No,<i> khanoum,</i>
     it's too heavy for you.

7
00:02:00.988 --> 00:02:03.388
 - Habibeh, you've been working
          since 5 a.m.

8
00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.390
       I can carry a cake.

9
00:02:05.392 --> 00:02:08.961
     - Navid, keep smiling,
 you might give me some nephews.

10
00:02:08.963 --> 00:02:10.596
        (Navid laughing)

11
00:02:10.598 --> 00:02:13.899
           -<i> Khanoum,</i>
 please let me take care of it.

12
00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:16.802
 - Hello. Hello. Oy! Thank you.
           Thank you.

13
00:02:16.804 --> 00:02:18.403
        (clinking glass)

14
00:02:18.405 --> 00:02:21.406
          Gather round.
   Don't worry, I won't sing.

15
00:02:21.408 --> 00:02:23.976
           I promise.
           (laughter)

16
00:02:23.978 --> 00:02:27.279
   Thank you. Thank you all...

17
00:02:27.281 --> 00:02:30.082
    for coming this evening.

18
00:02:30.084 --> 00:02:33.185
      I guess the last year
           has been...

19
00:02:33.187 --> 00:02:35.020
          challenging.

20
00:02:35.022 --> 00:02:37.189
     It's one way to put it.

21
00:02:37.191 --> 00:02:40.826
Very challenging, for all of us.
           But, uh...

22
00:02:40.828 --> 00:02:43.529
        we're still here,
     and we're celebrating.

23
00:02:44.632 --> 00:02:48.500
         And we have you
     to thank for that, son.

24
00:02:49.436 --> 00:02:52.137
You and that hard head of yours.
           (laughter)

25
00:02:52.139 --> 00:02:54.206
         I can just hear
        your grandfather.

26
00:02:54.208 --> 00:02:56.008
     If he were still here,

27
00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:58.544
       he would be saying
    the same thing about me.

28
00:02:59.446 --> 00:03:03.182
     Now you're on your way
 to boarding school in the U.S.

29
00:03:05.052 --> 00:03:07.486
    I think we told you that
  we needed to think about it.

30
00:03:07.488 --> 00:03:09.555
          - And I said,
"Don't you even dream about it."

31
00:03:09.557 --> 00:03:11.557
           (laughter)
     - And in the meantime,

32
00:03:11.559 --> 00:03:15.227
    he did what any young man
  with a good, uh, you know...

33
00:03:15.229 --> 00:03:17.396
         Did what I did
      when I was your age.

34
00:03:17.398 --> 00:03:19.131
        You took matters
      into your own hands.

35
00:03:19.133 --> 00:03:22.534
     And I couldn't possibly
         be more proud.

36
00:03:25.039 --> 00:03:28.040
       So... here we are.
           (chuckling)

37
00:03:28.042 --> 00:03:31.009
    Sending Parviz off to...

38
00:03:31.011 --> 00:03:33.979
        Deerfield Academy
        in Massachusetts.

39
00:03:35.983 --> 00:03:38.350
    Travel safe. Study hard.

40
00:03:38.352 --> 00:03:41.053
 - And don't you dare come home
       with a cowboy hat.

41
00:03:41.055 --> 00:03:43.055
           (laughter)

42
00:03:43.057 --> 00:03:45.557
           -<i> L'chaim.</i>
         (all):<i> L'chaim!</i>

43
00:03:55.069 --> 00:03:58.370
       -<i> Just eight months</i>
    <i> since the Shah fled Iran,</i>

44
00:03:58.372 --> 00:04:01.273
    <i> the Ayatollah Khomeini</i>
<i>and his Islamic revolutionaries</i>

45
00:04:01.275 --> 00:04:04.710
     <i> have consolidated power</i>
  <i> and transformed the country.</i>

46
00:04:04.712 --> 00:04:06.712
 <i> Sharia law now rules the land,</i>

47
00:04:06.714 --> 00:04:09.715
  <i> and a rising tide of violence</i>
        <i> is now targeting</i>

48
00:04:09.717 --> 00:04:12.017
     <i> many of the very groups</i>

49
00:04:12.019 --> 00:04:14.119
           <i> that helped</i>
     <i> the revolution abound.</i>

50
00:04:14.121 --> 00:04:16.255
      <i> Students, socialists,</i>
   <i> intellectuals and, indeed,</i>

51
00:04:16.257 --> 00:04:20.092
  <i> just about anyone who is not</i>
   <i> an Islamic fundamentalist.</i>

52
00:04:20.094 --> 00:04:23.228
  <i> Revolutionary Guards are now</i>
   <i> running the city of Tehran.</i>

53
00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:25.731
  - Come on, baby, let's go up.

54
00:04:25.733 --> 00:04:29.101
        - All that needs
      is a match and: boom!

55
00:04:31.739 --> 00:04:33.205
               Oy.

56
00:04:33.207 --> 00:04:35.540
   Do you really not feel it?

57
00:04:35.542 --> 00:04:37.476
      Or you don't want to?

58
00:04:37.478 --> 00:04:40.145
       That we're sitting
         on a time bomb.

59
00:04:40.147 --> 00:04:42.614
- You see what that does to you?

60
00:04:42.616 --> 00:04:46.551
     It's not good for you.
    You get totally wound up.

61
00:04:46.553 --> 00:04:50.322
     - Wound up! Our country
  is coming apart at the seams!

62
00:04:50.324 --> 00:04:52.658
   - Please, Isaac, not again.

63
00:04:54.128 --> 00:04:56.395
    - Open your eyes, Farnaz!

64
00:04:58.265 --> 00:05:00.332
         Take it all in.

65
00:05:00.334 --> 00:05:02.567
   Because at some point soon

66
00:05:02.569 --> 00:05:06.938
       we're going to need
     to leave it all behind.

67
00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:09.141
   - Mama, Baba! Are you okay?

68
00:05:09.143 --> 00:05:11.443
  - We're alright, sweetheart.

69
00:05:11.445 --> 00:05:13.512
        - What happened?

70
00:05:13.514 --> 00:05:15.981
   - Must've been a bad tube.

71
00:05:15.983 --> 00:05:17.649
             - Yeah.

72
00:05:18.819 --> 00:05:22.154
    - I, uh... have to...
       finish my packing.

73
00:05:22.156 --> 00:05:23.922
             - Okay.

74
00:05:23.924 --> 00:05:26.892
          - Good night.
          - Good night.

75
00:05:31.665 --> 00:05:33.665
          (soft music)

76
00:05:36.704 --> 00:05:39.037
        -<i> In a shift away</i>
      <i> from its declaration</i>

77
00:05:39.039 --> 00:05:41.039
       <i> that the government</i>
        <i> would not include</i>

78
00:05:41.041 --> 00:05:42.708
        <i> a supreme Islamic</i>
         <i> clerical ruler,</i>

79
00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.376
    <i> the Ayatollah has claimed</i>

80
00:05:44.378 --> 00:05:46.378
      <i> that the Guardianship</i>
      <i> of Islamic Jurists--</i>

81
00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:48.814
      - Habibeh, would you
     turn that off, please?

82
00:05:48.816 --> 00:05:50.615
         - Yes,<i> khanoum.</i>

83
00:05:50.617 --> 00:05:53.552
 -<i> Changes to the newly proposed</i>
         <i> constitution--</i>

84
00:05:58.025 --> 00:05:59.891
       - We need to talk.

85
00:06:01.795 --> 00:06:03.362
     I'll be home for lunch.

86
00:06:03.364 --> 00:06:05.364
      - Good. At what time?

87
00:06:05.366 --> 00:06:07.466
         - One o'clock.
             - Okay.

88
00:06:08.369 --> 00:06:10.902
       What about my kiss?

89
00:06:11.839 --> 00:06:13.905
          - Bye, Baba.
             - Bye.

90
00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:18.477
         (crowd roaring)

91
00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:24.449
        (crowd chanting)

92
00:06:29.523 --> 00:06:31.723
        - Lock your door.

93
00:06:59.887 --> 00:07:01.920
  Go on, you're gonna be late.

94
00:07:04.024 --> 00:07:06.158
       Shirin, your scarf.

95
00:07:09.696 --> 00:07:11.663
           How pretty.

96
00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:32.918
    - Hmm. Beautiful, Harad.

97
00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:35.554
       - Thank you, boss.
             - Hmm.

98
00:07:36.723 --> 00:07:38.890
           Excellent.

99
00:08:04.785 --> 00:08:07.018
       No, we're actually
       ahead of schedule.

100
00:08:07.955 --> 00:08:10.789
   Yes, we'll ship the orders
            tomorrow.

101
00:08:10.791 --> 00:08:12.958
           Thank you.
       Mm-hmm, thank you.

102
00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:15.594
   Likewise. A pleasure. Bye.

103
00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:18.096
         - Brother Amin,

104
00:08:18.098 --> 00:08:21.433
       we're here by order
  of the Revolutionary Guards.

105
00:08:22.269 --> 00:08:24.402
You're under arrest, brother.

106
00:08:30.777 --> 00:08:32.811
    - May I see your papers?

107
00:08:32.813 --> 00:08:34.946
    - Brother, don't concern
      yourself with papers.

108
00:08:34.948 --> 00:08:37.282
  You're Brother Amin, correct?

109
00:08:38.185 --> 00:08:40.085
            - Yes.
      - Then come with us.

110
00:08:43.357 --> 00:08:45.056
             <i> Yalla.</i>

111
00:08:53.901 --> 00:08:56.067
     (soft, dramatic music)

112
00:09:52.125 --> 00:09:53.925
         (crowd roaring)

113
00:10:37.237 --> 00:10:39.137
        (PA announcement)

114
00:10:52.686 --> 00:10:55.086
      - I'm Brother Mohsen.

115
00:10:55.088 --> 00:10:57.355
        Please follow me.

116
00:11:12.506 --> 00:11:14.205
           (coughing)

117
00:11:25.152 --> 00:11:26.785
          Have a seat.

118
00:11:29.556 --> 00:11:32.023
    Not there, the other one.

119
00:11:53.547 --> 00:11:55.547
              So...

120
00:11:55.549 --> 00:11:57.549
         Brother Amin...

121
00:11:57.551 --> 00:11:59.484
     what exactly do you do?

122
00:11:59.486 --> 00:12:00.985
             - Ahem.

123
00:12:00.987 --> 00:12:03.755
        I'm a gemologist,
         and a jeweller.

124
00:12:03.757 --> 00:12:05.523
             - Hmm.

125
00:12:05.525 --> 00:12:09.394
    Our records show that you
  travel to Israel quite a bit.

126
00:12:09.396 --> 00:12:11.196
        Is that correct?

127
00:12:11.198 --> 00:12:13.264
             - Yes.
           - What for?

128
00:12:14.768 --> 00:12:16.735
      - Well, sir, I have--

129
00:12:16.737 --> 00:12:18.737
   - Please, call me brother.

130
00:12:21.575 --> 00:12:24.576
  - I have family in Israel...

131
00:12:24.578 --> 00:12:26.778
            Brother.

132
00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:30.048
    There are no laws against
   traveling there, are there?

133
00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:32.584
   - Brother, are you familiar
        with the Mossad?

134
00:12:32.586 --> 00:12:36.354
     - I have nothing to do
    with government affairs,

135
00:12:36.356 --> 00:12:39.657
          neither here
    nor in any other country.

136
00:12:40.594 --> 00:12:44.562
        I'm a businessman
    who happens to be a Jew,

137
00:12:44.564 --> 00:12:46.431
          that is all.

138
00:12:46.433 --> 00:12:48.233
     - It's not that simple.

139
00:12:48.235 --> 00:12:51.536
    Tell me about your wife.

140
00:12:51.538 --> 00:12:53.538
       Farnaz Amin, right?

141
00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:56.040
      Wh-what does she do?

142
00:12:56.042 --> 00:12:58.076
      - She's a housewife.

143
00:12:58.078 --> 00:12:59.611
            - Really?

144
00:12:59.613 --> 00:13:01.279
             Then...

145
00:13:01.281 --> 00:13:03.314
          who is this?

146
00:13:04.384 --> 00:13:08.086
    I believe it says here
          Farnaz Amin?

147
00:13:08.088 --> 00:13:10.255
      This is not correct?

148
00:13:10.257 --> 00:13:14.492
 - She used to write an article
        here and there...

149
00:13:14.494 --> 00:13:17.762
 - This skating rink was a haven
      for sin, you realize,

150
00:13:17.764 --> 00:13:21.499
        and this article
is a piece of propaganda for it.

151
00:13:21.501 --> 00:13:23.501
 - No, it's not what you think.

152
00:13:23.503 --> 00:13:26.404
      She just wrote about
  what was going on around her.

153
00:13:26.406 --> 00:13:28.239
           Brother...

154
00:13:28.241 --> 00:13:31.109
         please tell me
       that she's alright.

155
00:13:31.111 --> 00:13:34.813
       - Too many factors
 play against you at the moment.

156
00:13:36.917 --> 00:13:38.716
            (ringing)

157
00:13:41.488 --> 00:13:43.288
            - Hello.
            -<i> Farnaz.</i>

158
00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:45.156
          - Ah, Navid!

159
00:13:45.158 --> 00:13:46.858
      Thank God you called.

160
00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:49.527
I have been trying to reach you.
         Where are you?

161
00:13:49.529 --> 00:13:52.363
 - It is better if I do not say.

162
00:13:52.365 --> 00:13:54.299
       - What do you mean?
       I can't find Isaac.

163
00:13:54.301 --> 00:13:56.668
           - Isaac...

164
00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:58.870
       has been arrested.

165
00:13:58.872 --> 00:14:01.439
       - How do you know?
        -<i> From my friend.</i>

166
00:14:01.441 --> 00:14:03.708
      He joined the Guards
          before this.

167
00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:07.111
           - But why?
 - You think they need a reason?

168
00:14:07.113 --> 00:14:09.781
   - Do you know where he is?
           - Not yet.

169
00:14:09.783 --> 00:14:12.116
   I will call you when I do.

170
00:14:12.118 --> 00:14:14.853
      -<i> You have to help me</i>
       <i> find your brother.</i>

171
00:14:14.855 --> 00:14:16.654
  -<i> They'll try and break him,</i>
             <i> Farnaz,</i>

172
00:14:16.656 --> 00:14:18.790
 <i> and then we'll all be at risk.</i>

173
00:14:18.792 --> 00:14:20.758
          I have to go.

174
00:14:21.962 --> 00:14:24.395
     (men groaning in pain)

175
00:14:37.544 --> 00:14:39.611
         (gate closing)

176
00:14:44.918 --> 00:14:46.384
           - I know...

177
00:14:46.386 --> 00:14:48.653
        it smells awful.

178
00:14:48.655 --> 00:14:50.188
         It's terrible.

179
00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:51.756
           I'm sorry.

180
00:14:51.758 --> 00:14:54.158
  My name is Mehdi, by the way.

181
00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:57.195
            - Isaac.
             - So...

182
00:14:57.197 --> 00:14:59.097
       how is it outside?

183
00:14:59.099 --> 00:15:01.165
           - Outside?

184
00:15:01.167 --> 00:15:04.335
           Since when?
  How long have you been here?

185
00:15:04.337 --> 00:15:06.905
  - Close to eight months now.

186
00:15:06.907 --> 00:15:09.007
         - Eight months.

187
00:15:11.177 --> 00:15:13.011
          (soft music)

188
00:15:16.082 --> 00:15:17.749
        -<i> Just remember,</i>

189
00:15:17.751 --> 00:15:21.586
   if they ask you questions,
   say the minimum necessary.

190
00:15:21.588 --> 00:15:24.355
         - Don't worry,
       Amin is a good man,

191
00:15:24.357 --> 00:15:26.824
      and he will get out.
          Praise Allah.

192
00:15:28.929 --> 00:15:33.264
   Every pilgrim goes to Mecca
          his own way.

193
00:15:34.434 --> 00:15:36.567
            - Sister?

194
00:15:36.569 --> 00:15:38.903
 - I am looking for my husband.

195
00:15:38.905 --> 00:15:41.706
  I was wondering if he's here.

196
00:15:41.708 --> 00:15:43.641
       - We don't give out
        such information.

197
00:15:43.643 --> 00:15:45.610
      - Brother, please...

198
00:15:45.612 --> 00:15:48.246
      I would like to know
         if he's alive.

199
00:15:48.248 --> 00:15:50.715
  He didn't come home from work
           last night.

200
00:15:50.717 --> 00:15:52.650
  - Maybe he had better things
             to do.

201
00:15:52.652 --> 00:15:54.986
     - I know plenty of men
           like that,

202
00:15:54.988 --> 00:15:57.655
         but Isaac Amin
       isn't one of them.

203
00:15:57.657 --> 00:15:59.691
         - Who is this?
         - I'm a friend.

204
00:16:01.561 --> 00:16:04.062
      - Alright, wait here.

205
00:16:05.131 --> 00:16:08.333
       - You see,<i> khanoum,</i>
 it's good that you brought me.

206
00:16:08.335 --> 00:16:10.902
        He liked the idea
       of someone like you

207
00:16:10.904 --> 00:16:12.870
  would have a friend like me.

208
00:16:15.642 --> 00:16:18.076
           - Come in.
      - It will be alright.

209
00:16:22.349 --> 00:16:24.082
         -<i> Yalla, yalla.</i>

210
00:16:51.678 --> 00:16:54.345
   (door opening and closing)

211
00:17:00.487 --> 00:17:02.020
            (gasping)

212
00:17:02.022 --> 00:17:04.355
       - State your name.

213
00:17:05.291 --> 00:17:07.358
        - Vartan Sofoyan.

214
00:17:11.564 --> 00:17:13.965
      - You know this man.

215
00:17:13.967 --> 00:17:15.867
       - I am afraid not.

216
00:17:15.869 --> 00:17:17.568
      - Then why the gasp?

217
00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:19.670
     - The hood, brother...

218
00:17:19.672 --> 00:17:21.773
         it startled me.

219
00:17:24.511 --> 00:17:25.943
           - Take him.

220
00:17:28.915 --> 00:17:30.782
           Follow me.

221
00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:09.287
       You know that man,
         Vartan Sofoyan.

222
00:18:09.289 --> 00:18:12.924
 - I said I didn't and I don't.

223
00:18:12.926 --> 00:18:17.695
   Brother, I am here looking
   for my husband, Isaac Amin.

224
00:18:17.697 --> 00:18:21.566
   - Sofoyan was good friends
     with the royal family.

225
00:18:21.568 --> 00:18:24.102
       He played for them
       on many occasions.

226
00:18:24.104 --> 00:18:27.438
      - I really would like
to find out where my husband is.

227
00:18:27.440 --> 00:18:30.108
  - You were once a journalist.

228
00:18:30.110 --> 00:18:32.310
      Is that not correct?

229
00:18:32.312 --> 00:18:34.445
 - I would not call myself that.

230
00:18:34.447 --> 00:18:36.614
    I wrote once in a while.

231
00:18:36.616 --> 00:18:39.083
       - A dabbler, then.
          - I suppose.

232
00:18:39.085 --> 00:18:43.588
   - Only those who can afford
     to be dabblers dabble.

233
00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:46.390
  Those who have to work, work.

234
00:18:46.392 --> 00:18:48.826
    - I could only afford it
      thanks to my husband,

235
00:18:48.828 --> 00:18:50.428
      who worked very hard.

236
00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:54.265
   - Yes, he worked very hard
    in amassing his fortune.

237
00:18:54.267 --> 00:18:56.400
 - He earned his money honestly.

238
00:18:56.402 --> 00:19:00.171
 - Tell me about these articles.
    - They were light pieces.

239
00:19:00.173 --> 00:19:02.406
       - I'm feeling light
    this morning. Indulge me.

240
00:19:02.408 --> 00:19:03.975
 - I wrote about foreign places.

241
00:19:03.977 --> 00:19:06.310
          - You touted
     the virtues of alcohol

242
00:19:06.312 --> 00:19:07.845
  and gushed about cathedrals.

243
00:19:07.847 --> 00:19:10.181
          Your articles
    were pieces of propaganda

244
00:19:10.183 --> 00:19:11.983
      for an indecent life.

245
00:19:11.985 --> 00:19:14.085
 - Why am I being interrogated?

246
00:19:14.087 --> 00:19:16.687
 I am not charged with anything.

247
00:19:18.424 --> 00:19:20.324
        Please, brother,

248
00:19:20.326 --> 00:19:23.261
  tell me where my husband is.

249
00:19:25.832 --> 00:19:29.433
   - It's time you understood,
          Sister Amin,

250
00:19:29.435 --> 00:19:32.370
         that the times
      when people like you

251
00:19:32.372 --> 00:19:36.007
   could demand things from us
            are over.

252
00:19:36.009 --> 00:19:38.209
             Now...

253
00:19:38.211 --> 00:19:39.977
         it is our turn.

254
00:19:39.979 --> 00:19:41.913
            Get out.

255
00:19:54.227 --> 00:19:56.894
 - Did they say anything to you?

256
00:19:56.896 --> 00:20:00.731
         - They asked me
 whether I like being a servant.

257
00:20:01.668 --> 00:20:04.535
   - What does that have to do
         with anything?

258
00:20:07.473 --> 00:20:10.541
 You're not letting these people
    put ideas into your head,

259
00:20:10.543 --> 00:20:12.043
        are you, Habibeh?

260
00:20:12.045 --> 00:20:16.881
       - No. No,<i> khanoum, </i>
         of course not.

261
00:20:16.883 --> 00:20:19.483
             - Good.
       - But I don't know.

262
00:20:19.485 --> 00:20:23.120
    My son says there's a lot
   that needs to be set right.

263
00:20:24.057 --> 00:20:27.491
   - What? Morteza has become
        a revolutionary?

264
00:20:27.493 --> 00:20:29.193
   - He has joined the Guards.

265
00:20:29.195 --> 00:20:31.562
   I didn't want to tell you,

266
00:20:31.564 --> 00:20:34.699
        because I thought
  you might get upset with me.

267
00:20:34.701 --> 00:20:38.369
    But when I listen to him,
    he makes a lot of sense.

268
00:20:38.371 --> 00:20:41.172
       - What does he say
    that makes so much sense?

269
00:20:41.174 --> 00:20:44.575
     - He says, "Why should
  some people live like kings,

270
00:20:44.577 --> 00:20:46.510
     and the rest like rats?

271
00:20:46.512 --> 00:20:48.512
   And why should the wealthy,

272
00:20:48.514 --> 00:20:51.616
      so crazy for the West
           and Europe,

273
00:20:51.618 --> 00:20:55.720
  decide how the whole country
   should dress, talk, live?"

274
00:20:55.722 --> 00:20:59.190
   What if we want our mullahs
 to rule us and not that saint?

275
00:20:59.192 --> 00:21:02.760
         Morteza told me
   he's worshipped in Europe.

276
00:21:02.762 --> 00:21:06.597
     I know. Saint-Laurent?
     Or something like that.

277
00:21:06.599 --> 00:21:09.467
      - Yves Saint-Laurent?
       - Yes, that's him.

278
00:21:09.469 --> 00:21:11.636
           (laughing)

279
00:21:13.573 --> 00:21:16.974
       - He's not a saint,
        he's a designer.

280
00:21:16.976 --> 00:21:18.909
    That is his actual name.

281
00:21:18.911 --> 00:21:20.544
       - You see,<i> khanoum?</i>

282
00:21:20.546 --> 00:21:23.080
         You put me down
      every chance you get.

283
00:21:23.082 --> 00:21:25.650
         - No, Habibeh,
    I'm not putting you down,

284
00:21:25.652 --> 00:21:27.551
       but you don't know
   what you're talking about.

285
00:21:27.553 --> 00:21:31.088
      You're just repeating
  some nonsense that you heard.

286
00:21:31.090 --> 00:21:33.457
           -<i> Khanoum, </i>
     you're doing it again.

287
00:21:33.459 --> 00:21:35.326
            (sighing)

288
00:21:35.328 --> 00:21:36.961
            - Sorry.

289
00:21:36.963 --> 00:21:39.163
    Habibeh, you're entitled
        to your feelings,

290
00:21:39.165 --> 00:21:42.933
      but what I ask of you
    is that you don't forget

291
00:21:42.935 --> 00:21:46.103
the friendship that we've shared
       for so many years.

292
00:21:46.105 --> 00:21:48.072
 - No,<i> khanoum,</i> I don't forget.

293
00:21:48.074 --> 00:21:50.341
    But am I a friend to you,

294
00:21:50.343 --> 00:21:53.077
    as Mr. Sofoyan is to you,
            and Amin?

295
00:21:53.079 --> 00:21:56.914
     You dine all together.
     You go to the theatre.

296
00:21:56.916 --> 00:21:58.582
        But in 20 years,

297
00:21:58.584 --> 00:22:01.319
  I have not even shared table
            with you.

298
00:22:14.367 --> 00:22:16.834
        (PA announcement)

299
00:22:16.836 --> 00:22:19.003
        (gates clanging)

300
00:22:19.005 --> 00:22:21.238
         (men shouting)

301
00:22:30.183 --> 00:22:32.116
        - Get used to it.

302
00:22:33.186 --> 00:22:36.253
  If they don't say your name,
           thank God.

303
00:22:37.390 --> 00:22:39.690
    If they do, say a prayer.

304
00:22:42.829 --> 00:22:44.695
         (gate clanging)

305
00:22:45.631 --> 00:22:47.465
      (indistinct chatter)

306
00:22:48.534 --> 00:22:51.469
    He knew his end was near.

307
00:22:51.471 --> 00:22:54.038
       - How did he know?

308
00:22:54.040 --> 00:22:55.706
         - He just did.

309
00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:00.478
      One develops a sense
        for these things.

310
00:23:01.414 --> 00:23:04.915
        You can smell it
 on your interrogator's breath.

311
00:23:05.852 --> 00:23:09.286
  You know when he's had enough
        to deal with you.

312
00:23:12.859 --> 00:23:14.725
         (men shouting)

313
00:23:20.900 --> 00:23:24.034
   -<i> Your father gave it to me</i>
      <i> when Parviz was born.</i>

314
00:23:24.036 --> 00:23:25.669
    He cut the stone himself.

315
00:23:25.671 --> 00:23:28.339
             - Okay,
 when were you last wearing it?

316
00:23:28.341 --> 00:23:30.608
          - For Parviz,
     at the farewell party.

317
00:23:30.610 --> 00:23:34.011
    - You're going to be late
    getting Shirin to school.

318
00:23:34.013 --> 00:23:36.680
    - Habibeh, have you seen
        my sapphire ring?

319
00:23:36.682 --> 00:23:40.084
 The one with the small diamonds
    around the centre stone?

320
00:23:40.086 --> 00:23:41.919
   - I'm afraid not,<i> khanoum.</i>

321
00:23:41.921 --> 00:23:45.356
       - It was just here.
 It did not walk out on its own.

322
00:23:46.259 --> 00:23:48.926
 - I'll keep an eye out for it.

323
00:23:49.862 --> 00:23:51.529
          - Thank you.

324
00:23:55.101 --> 00:23:57.368
  -<i> Tell me about your brother,</i>
             <i> Navid.</i>

325
00:23:59.472 --> 00:24:02.807
        - I'm not really
     all that close to him.

326
00:24:02.809 --> 00:24:06.977
   - Well, it may interest you
to know that he has a new job...

327
00:24:06.979 --> 00:24:08.646
         smuggling vodka
        into the country.

328
00:24:08.648 --> 00:24:11.382
 Well, if... in fact my brother

329
00:24:11.384 --> 00:24:13.717
           is involved
      with smuggling vodka,

330
00:24:13.719 --> 00:24:15.586
  I have nothing to do with it.

331
00:24:15.588 --> 00:24:19.390
     - You know, I like you,
        for some reason,

332
00:24:19.392 --> 00:24:23.093
     and I want to help you,
    but I can't do it alone.

333
00:24:23.095 --> 00:24:24.562
      You have to help me.

334
00:24:25.731 --> 00:24:28.132
            You think
     he'll get away with it?

335
00:24:28.134 --> 00:24:29.934
       You and your family
         of libertines,

336
00:24:29.936 --> 00:24:32.102
            you think
   you can protect each other?

337
00:24:32.104 --> 00:24:35.105
    - Perhaps there has been
          some mistake.

338
00:24:35.107 --> 00:24:37.641
     - The mistake, brother,
            is yours.

339
00:24:37.643 --> 00:24:40.311
        You seem to think
   this is some kind of game.

340
00:24:40.313 --> 00:24:42.146
          - No, no, no.

341
00:24:42.148 --> 00:24:46.383
     - Then you will tell me
 where I can find your brother.

342
00:24:49.155 --> 00:24:53.157
        - Look, brother,
     I am a simple man. I...

343
00:24:53.159 --> 00:24:56.026
 My preoccupations are my work,

344
00:24:56.028 --> 00:24:58.963
   and my wife, my daughter--

345
00:24:58.965 --> 00:25:00.831
            - Simple?

346
00:25:00.833 --> 00:25:05.135
   I suppose figuring out all
  your bank accounts is simple.

347
00:25:05.137 --> 00:25:08.172
           I, for one,
  had trouble following it all.

348
00:25:08.174 --> 00:25:11.642
        I'd say it takes
   a pretty sophisticated mind

349
00:25:11.644 --> 00:25:13.978
          to carry out
     all these transactions.

350
00:25:13.980 --> 00:25:16.547
  - Sophisticated in business,
           yes, but--

351
00:25:16.549 --> 00:25:19.717
  - Listen to me, listen to me!

352
00:25:19.719 --> 00:25:22.453
  We know everything about you.

353
00:25:22.455 --> 00:25:25.689
 What you stock in your pantry!

354
00:25:25.691 --> 00:25:30.327
     Even the kind of cognac
    your wife likes to drink!

355
00:25:30.329 --> 00:25:31.996
            (sighing)

356
00:25:31.998 --> 00:25:34.431
 How sad it should come to this.

357
00:25:36.369 --> 00:25:38.435
              Here.

358
00:25:47.013 --> 00:25:48.579
         Help yourself.

359
00:25:48.581 --> 00:25:51.282
   We may be here a long time.

360
00:26:03.329 --> 00:26:05.462
       What's the matter?

361
00:26:09.402 --> 00:26:11.702
     - I... I need a light.

362
00:26:11.704 --> 00:26:16.073
- Well, then, brother, just ask.
 And I'd like the same from you.

363
00:26:16.075 --> 00:26:18.108
  When I ask you for something,

364
00:26:18.110 --> 00:26:21.912
   I'd like to get it without
   too much difficulty. Come.

365
00:26:26.052 --> 00:26:27.718
           (screaming)

366
00:26:27.720 --> 00:26:30.621
      You can make it stop.
      You can make it stop!

367
00:26:30.623 --> 00:26:32.923
   (screaming, then groaning)

368
00:26:36.696 --> 00:26:38.429
              - Ah!

369
00:26:38.431 --> 00:26:40.598
            (panting)

370
00:26:42.268 --> 00:26:44.368
           (grunting)

371
00:26:46.072 --> 00:26:47.938
            (sobbing)

372
00:26:49.709 --> 00:26:51.508
           (screaming)

373
00:26:53.779 --> 00:26:56.180
         (phone ringing)

374
00:26:59.285 --> 00:27:00.951
            - Hello.

375
00:27:00.953 --> 00:27:04.922
        - Mama, it's me.
            - Parviz.

376
00:27:04.924 --> 00:27:08.158
 - I'm just, uh... I'm checking
       to see how you are.

377
00:27:08.160 --> 00:27:10.761
         - It is so good
       to hear your voice.

378
00:27:10.763 --> 00:27:13.063
   - And how is Shirin doing?
          - She's fine.

379
00:27:13.065 --> 00:27:15.099
           - And Baba?
            - He's...

380
00:27:15.101 --> 00:27:18.435
    he's still at the office,
          working late.

381
00:27:18.437 --> 00:27:20.571
       Listen, sweetheart,
       would it be alright

382
00:27:20.573 --> 00:27:24.508
    if I call you back later?
     I am expecting a call.

383
00:27:24.510 --> 00:27:26.276
          - Okay, sure.

384
00:27:26.278 --> 00:27:28.112
         - We love you.

385
00:27:28.114 --> 00:27:30.147
       - I love you, too.

386
00:27:30.149 --> 00:27:32.816
        (mournful music)

387
00:27:32.818 --> 00:27:34.752
           (dial tone)

388
00:27:42.495 --> 00:27:44.561
        (mournful music)

389
00:27:49.702 --> 00:27:51.769
    - Good morning,<i> khanoum.</i>

390
00:27:52.505 --> 00:27:54.872
         - Good morning.

391
00:27:55.708 --> 00:27:57.608
       - Are you alright?

392
00:27:57.610 --> 00:27:59.510
            - Yeah...

393
00:27:59.512 --> 00:28:01.612
         I'm getting up.

394
00:28:03.516 --> 00:28:07.418
    - This practice,<i> khanoum,</i>
       will have to stop.

395
00:28:09.955 --> 00:28:12.156
   - Oh, I only had one glass.

396
00:28:12.158 --> 00:28:13.657
       - One glass or 10,

397
00:28:13.659 --> 00:28:16.160
     it makes no difference.

398
00:28:16.162 --> 00:28:18.228
       It is illegal now.

399
00:28:25.371 --> 00:28:27.137
       - Is that a threat?

400
00:28:27.139 --> 00:28:29.406
  - It's just a fact,<i> khanoum.</i>

401
00:28:29.408 --> 00:28:32.443
           - The fact
    is that this is my house.

402
00:28:34.547 --> 00:28:37.181
    And today is Wednesday...

403
00:28:37.183 --> 00:28:40.050
         so don't forget
      to wash the windows.

404
00:28:40.052 --> 00:28:41.618
         - Yes,<i> khanoum.</i>

405
00:29:04.210 --> 00:29:05.676
            - Isaac.

406
00:29:07.580 --> 00:29:10.013
            - Barton.

407
00:29:10.015 --> 00:29:11.949
         Vartan Sofoyan.

408
00:29:12.785 --> 00:29:14.485
             My God.

409
00:29:15.788 --> 00:29:17.421
        Three weeks ago,

410
00:29:17.423 --> 00:29:19.356
    you were teaching Shirin
       to play the violin.

411
00:29:19.358 --> 00:29:21.091
            I wish...

412
00:29:23.028 --> 00:29:26.163
       (PA):<i> All prisoners</i>
     <i> go back to your cells.</i>

413
00:29:41.046 --> 00:29:43.213
 - Farnaz, please take it easy,
          okay? Please!

414
00:29:43.215 --> 00:29:46.617
- Sorry, but nobody's picking up
    the phone in this place.

415
00:29:46.619 --> 00:29:48.819
        Why is that for?
        - Just calm down.

416
00:29:48.821 --> 00:29:51.255
      - I don't understand
        what's going on.

417
00:29:51.257 --> 00:29:52.923
         (man shouting)

418
00:29:52.925 --> 00:29:55.559
    Talia, what is happening?
       What are you doing?

419
00:29:55.561 --> 00:29:58.829
      - Hey, hey, hey, hey.
 Everything's okay, don't worry.

420
00:29:58.831 --> 00:30:00.831
           - Morteza,
     what is going on here?

421
00:30:00.833 --> 00:30:03.500
  - Nothing, we're just trying
to move the equipment and stones

422
00:30:03.502 --> 00:30:05.269
   to a more secure location.
          - The stones?

423
00:30:05.271 --> 00:30:07.004
        - To protect them
    from the revolutionaries.

424
00:30:07.006 --> 00:30:09.406
     We think they may want
         to seize them.

425
00:30:09.408 --> 00:30:10.841
          - Is that so?
             - Yes.

426
00:30:10.843 --> 00:30:12.843
     - And how do you know?

427
00:30:12.845 --> 00:30:15.646
       - Now listen to me,
         trust me, okay?

428
00:30:15.648 --> 00:30:17.648
    I just want to help you.

429
00:30:17.650 --> 00:30:19.483
       Wait, wait, please.

430
00:30:19.485 --> 00:30:21.618
    - We would like to go in.

431
00:30:21.620 --> 00:30:23.654
   - No, you cannot go in now.
           Just leave.

432
00:30:23.656 --> 00:30:25.489
     - Where are you taking
           everything?

433
00:30:25.491 --> 00:30:27.191
 - To a safe place. Now go home.

434
00:30:27.193 --> 00:30:29.293
  You must have more important
     things to take care of.

435
00:30:29.295 --> 00:30:30.994
         - I'm going in.
              - No.

436
00:30:30.996 --> 00:30:34.464
      You're not going in.
     I'm asking you nicely.

437
00:30:34.466 --> 00:30:37.201
    Don't let this get nasty.
        I'm telling you--

438
00:30:37.203 --> 00:30:39.236
           (screaming)
            - Farnaz!

439
00:30:41.307 --> 00:30:43.507
             Farnaz!
         (man shouting)

440
00:30:43.509 --> 00:30:47.444
   Whoa, let me go, let me go.
       Farnaz, be careful!

441
00:30:47.446 --> 00:30:49.279
    - What is going on here?

442
00:30:49.281 --> 00:30:51.215
          Farhanika...

443
00:30:52.718 --> 00:30:55.152
    ...can you explain this?
      - I'm sorry,<i> khanoum,</i>

444
00:30:55.154 --> 00:30:56.987
 things have gotten out of hand.

445
00:30:56.989 --> 00:31:00.624
I tried to talk sense into them,
      but there was no use.

446
00:31:00.626 --> 00:31:03.360
    They said... I was blind
     to all the exploitation

447
00:31:03.362 --> 00:31:05.529
 that's been going on for years.

448
00:31:05.531 --> 00:31:07.331
         - Exploitation?
          - They said--

449
00:31:07.333 --> 00:31:09.132
         - These people
   were all unemployed gypsies

450
00:31:09.134 --> 00:31:10.634
   when my husband hired them.

451
00:31:10.636 --> 00:31:13.003
        He took them in,
    paid for their education.

452
00:31:13.005 --> 00:31:15.072
      Is this what you call
         exploitation?!

453
00:31:15.074 --> 00:31:17.174
 - They weren't exactly gypsies,
            <i> khanoum.</i>

454
00:31:17.176 --> 00:31:19.977
     They might have lacked
  education, but we weren't...

455
00:31:19.979 --> 00:31:23.080
          - I'm sorry,
   I did not mean it that way,

456
00:31:23.082 --> 00:31:25.215
    especially not about you.

457
00:31:25.217 --> 00:31:28.385
       It's just that I...
       I don't understand.

458
00:31:29.355 --> 00:31:31.922
    Why are they doing this?

459
00:31:31.924 --> 00:31:35.726
       How can they forget
everything that he did for them?

460
00:31:35.728 --> 00:31:37.527
     - That's how it is now.

461
00:31:37.529 --> 00:31:39.763
         Sorry,<i> khanoum.</i>
   - Have you lost your mind?

462
00:31:39.765 --> 00:31:42.733
        This is not fair.
  He hasn't had his trial yet.

463
00:31:42.735 --> 00:31:44.368
      Farnaz, are you okay?
            - Trial?

464
00:31:44.370 --> 00:31:47.271
        If you guys think
  there's going to be a trial,

465
00:31:47.273 --> 00:31:49.172
       you're going to be
       very disappointed.

466
00:31:53.379 --> 00:31:55.746
          - Morteza...

467
00:31:55.748 --> 00:31:57.748
     why are you doing this?

468
00:31:57.750 --> 00:32:00.817
   Was my husband bad to you?

469
00:32:02.187 --> 00:32:04.755
Did he ever refuse you anything?

470
00:32:04.757 --> 00:32:07.024
      - You see,<i> khanoum...</i>

471
00:32:08.594 --> 00:32:11.028
   ...you fail to understand.

472
00:32:11.897 --> 00:32:14.398
     I mean that sincerely.

473
00:32:14.400 --> 00:32:18.135
            You see,
 this isn't just about one man.

474
00:32:18.137 --> 00:32:20.270
 It's about a collection of men.

475
00:32:20.272 --> 00:32:23.774
    Men who turned their back
          on injustice.

476
00:32:23.776 --> 00:32:27.377
        Men who profited
     from a corrupt regime.

477
00:32:27.379 --> 00:32:30.314
   Men who built their villas

478
00:32:30.316 --> 00:32:33.317
          and traveled
      whenever they wished

479
00:32:33.319 --> 00:32:37.621
  to places the likes of us...
  didn't even dare to dream of.

480
00:32:37.623 --> 00:32:41.959
      Have you ever thought
    about how we lived? Huh?

481
00:32:41.961 --> 00:32:48.231
 Why does a country with so much
   give so little to the poor?

482
00:32:48.233 --> 00:32:52.169
        You never cared.
 But that's okay. You know why?

483
00:32:52.171 --> 00:32:55.772
    Because God has answered
     the prayer of the weak.

484
00:32:55.774 --> 00:32:59.009
       God is on the side
        of the faithful,

485
00:32:59.011 --> 00:33:01.912
       not on the sinners.
       God will forever--

486
00:33:01.914 --> 00:33:03.613
          - Since when
      are you so faithful?

487
00:33:03.615 --> 00:33:05.315
   Just a couple of years ago,

488
00:33:05.317 --> 00:33:07.651
        you would show up
      with your tight jeans

489
00:33:07.653 --> 00:33:11.555
  and borrow our car to pick up
  one of your five girlfriends.

490
00:33:12.825 --> 00:33:16.493
      You think that beard
    makes you a man of God?!

491
00:33:16.495 --> 00:33:18.362
  - Farnaz, come on, let's go.
         That's enough.

492
00:33:18.364 --> 00:33:21.164
  - And since when is stealing
      people's possessions

493
00:33:21.166 --> 00:33:22.833
        the call of God?

494
00:33:22.835 --> 00:33:24.701
     You are all hypocrites

495
00:33:24.703 --> 00:33:26.770
        who have suddenly
         come into power

496
00:33:26.772 --> 00:33:29.573
and don't know how to handle it.

497
00:34:04.309 --> 00:34:06.510
        - Does anyone...

498
00:34:06.512 --> 00:34:08.712
       remember a time...

499
00:34:08.714 --> 00:34:10.547
        when this country

500
00:34:10.549 --> 00:34:12.349
            was just?
            Generous?

501
00:34:12.351 --> 00:34:14.184
       - Cyrus the Great.

502
00:34:14.186 --> 00:34:16.386
      - We were all equal.

503
00:34:18.090 --> 00:34:19.890
            Muslim...

504
00:34:19.892 --> 00:34:22.726
          Christian...

505
00:34:22.728 --> 00:34:25.095
             Jew...

506
00:34:25.097 --> 00:34:26.963
         Didn't matter.

507
00:34:29.334 --> 00:34:31.401
     We were a great empire.

508
00:34:32.337 --> 00:34:35.572
     - Oh, Baba-ji, please.

509
00:34:35.574 --> 00:34:37.741
       That's the problem
       with this country.

510
00:34:37.743 --> 00:34:39.576
 We somehow think we're special,

511
00:34:39.578 --> 00:34:42.079
    because once upon a time
         we were great.

512
00:34:42.081 --> 00:34:44.748
         Darius, Cyrus,

513
00:34:44.750 --> 00:34:46.550
          Persepolis...

514
00:34:46.552 --> 00:34:49.453
    That was 2,500 years ago.

515
00:34:49.455 --> 00:34:51.555
        What are we now?

516
00:34:51.557 --> 00:34:53.123
              Huh?

517
00:34:53.125 --> 00:34:54.991
           Barbarians.

518
00:34:56.562 --> 00:34:58.128
             - No...

519
00:34:58.130 --> 00:34:59.930
           (sniffling)

520
00:34:59.932 --> 00:35:01.832
         Not all of us.

521
00:35:06.538 --> 00:35:09.106
<i>You're gonna throw this to them</i>
       <i> or get a picture?</i>

522
00:35:09.108 --> 00:35:10.774
           -<i> Not yet.</i>
    -<i> Take a picture for her.</i>

523
00:35:10.776 --> 00:35:12.909
   -<i> Ah! Wait... maybe a pin--</i>

524
00:35:12.911 --> 00:35:14.711
     -<i> Sorry, sorry, sorry.</i>

525
00:35:14.713 --> 00:35:16.213
             - Mama!

526
00:35:18.417 --> 00:35:20.784
       What happened here?

527
00:35:20.786 --> 00:35:23.787
      - I looked everywhere
         for that ring.

528
00:35:23.789 --> 00:35:26.289
       It's just not here.

529
00:35:26.291 --> 00:35:28.492
               No.

530
00:35:32.598 --> 00:35:34.631
           (laughing)
     - Look at Baba's head.

531
00:35:34.633 --> 00:35:36.600
           -<i> Yes, yes.</i>

532
00:35:36.602 --> 00:35:38.401
           (laughter)

533
00:35:38.403 --> 00:35:40.170
       - And look at you.

534
00:35:40.172 --> 00:35:41.972
      You're so beautiful.

535
00:35:43.809 --> 00:35:45.876
     - You're so beautiful.

536
00:35:51.183 --> 00:35:53.016
     - What's he doing that?

537
00:35:53.018 --> 00:35:55.986
  - He's stepping on the glass.
           - What for?

538
00:35:55.988 --> 00:35:58.655
   - It's to remind us that...

539
00:35:58.657 --> 00:36:01.358
   even in times of great joy,

540
00:36:01.360 --> 00:36:03.260
        there is sadness.

541
00:36:03.262 --> 00:36:05.829
      That love is fragile.

542
00:36:05.831 --> 00:36:08.498
          It can break
     if you're not careful.

543
00:36:14.840 --> 00:36:16.439
         Shirin-joon...

544
00:36:19.978 --> 00:36:21.444
         At some point,

545
00:36:21.446 --> 00:36:23.747
      Guards will be coming
      to search the house.

546
00:36:24.650 --> 00:36:27.150
       We have to get rid
           of anything

547
00:36:27.152 --> 00:36:29.653
  that could look incriminating
         to your father.

548
00:36:29.655 --> 00:36:32.656
    The same way that you had
to tear the pictures of the Shah

549
00:36:32.658 --> 00:36:34.090
    from your school books...

550
00:36:35.861 --> 00:36:38.094
 ...all of this will have to go.

551
00:36:51.243 --> 00:36:53.109
           (laughing)

552
00:36:55.681 --> 00:36:57.247
        (Shirin laughing)

553
00:36:57.249 --> 00:37:00.016
    That is your Uncle Navid
    when he was a little boy.

554
00:37:00.018 --> 00:37:02.385
           (laughing)

555
00:37:10.262 --> 00:37:12.562
             - Mama?

556
00:37:12.564 --> 00:37:14.598
     - Believe it or not...

557
00:37:16.902 --> 00:37:19.903
       ...September 1958,

558
00:37:19.905 --> 00:37:22.439
  when I first met your father
           in Shiraz.

559
00:37:22.441 --> 00:37:26.509
  - "My breath is narrowed down
        to one long sigh

560
00:37:26.511 --> 00:37:30.280
   for a red mouth that burns
     my thoughts like fire."

561
00:37:30.282 --> 00:37:32.582
         - Give me that.

562
00:37:32.584 --> 00:37:35.986
       - Baba wrote that.
    - It is his handwriting.

563
00:37:37.089 --> 00:37:39.289
   The words belong to Hafiz.

564
00:37:39.291 --> 00:37:41.992
       - It's about love?
             - Yeah.

565
00:37:43.362 --> 00:37:44.861
        - Let me read it.

566
00:37:54.740 --> 00:37:57.741
   "My breath is narrowed down
        to one long sigh

567
00:37:57.743 --> 00:38:01.278
   "For a red mouth that burns
    my thoughts like a fire.

568
00:38:01.280 --> 00:38:05.115
<i>"When will that mouth draw near</i>
        <i> and make reply</i>

569
00:38:05.117 --> 00:38:08.618
        <i> To one whose life</i>
   <i> is straitened with desire?"</i>

570
00:38:12.557 --> 00:38:14.624
        (mournful music)

571
00:38:23.769 --> 00:38:25.568
        (Farnaz laughing)
             - Huh?

572
00:38:25.570 --> 00:38:27.337
        (Isaac chuckling)

573
00:38:27.339 --> 00:38:30.140
       - It is beautiful!
           (laughter)

574
00:38:30.142 --> 00:38:32.776
      Look at the kitchen!

575
00:38:32.778 --> 00:38:35.145
       - Hmm? You like it?

576
00:38:35.147 --> 00:38:37.981
       - Can we afford it?
             - Yes.

577
00:38:37.983 --> 00:38:39.849
           (laughter)

578
00:38:42.354 --> 00:38:44.587
     - Oh... it's beautiful!

579
00:38:44.589 --> 00:38:46.356
         It's beautiful!

580
00:38:46.358 --> 00:38:48.358
  - Want to see the best part?
             - Yes.

581
00:38:48.360 --> 00:38:52.162
 - The bedroom. No, I'm kidding.
   It's not that, but come on.

582
00:38:52.164 --> 00:38:55.365
     Okay. Close your eyes.

583
00:38:55.367 --> 00:38:57.600
           Keep... No!
       (Farnaz exclaiming)

584
00:38:57.602 --> 00:38:59.602
              Yeah.
           (chuckling)

585
00:38:59.604 --> 00:39:02.839
    - Oh, a reflecting pool.
     - It needs some water.

586
00:39:02.841 --> 00:39:07.310
 You always talked about the one
    you had growing up. Hmm?

587
00:39:07.312 --> 00:39:10.180
  What was it you used to say?

588
00:39:10.182 --> 00:39:14.017
      "I could always count
   on its simplified beauty."

589
00:39:14.019 --> 00:39:15.685
       (chuckling softly)

590
00:39:20.392 --> 00:39:22.459
      - Tell the pass code!

591
00:39:24.396 --> 00:39:26.830
             Hurry!

592
00:39:26.832 --> 00:39:28.832
            (banging)

593
00:39:28.834 --> 00:39:30.900
       Tell the pass code!

594
00:39:32.838 --> 00:39:34.471
             Hurry!

595
00:39:40.045 --> 00:39:42.479
           We are here
      to search your house.

596
00:39:49.855 --> 00:39:51.721
        Hurry! Take that.

597
00:39:51.723 --> 00:39:53.656
         Move. Take it.

598
00:39:53.658 --> 00:39:56.226
        - Shirin. Shirin?

599
00:39:56.228 --> 00:39:58.128
            Shirin...

600
00:40:09.541 --> 00:40:11.141
            - Radio!

601
00:40:20.452 --> 00:40:22.318
            - Shirin.

602
00:40:49.481 --> 00:40:51.448
       I have to go check
         on my daughter.

603
00:40:51.450 --> 00:40:53.917
  - You're not going anywhere.
      - I'll be right back.

604
00:40:53.919 --> 00:40:55.985
    - I'm sure your daughter
          is fine. Sit!

605
00:41:35.961 --> 00:41:38.161
            The ring.

606
00:41:38.163 --> 00:41:41.231
         Give it to me,
       or I'll cut it off.

607
00:41:50.175 --> 00:41:52.242
       Give it to me now!

608
00:41:56.548 --> 00:41:58.414
            (crying)

609
00:42:08.226 --> 00:42:09.926
             - Mama!

610
00:42:11.363 --> 00:42:13.062
        - Where were you?

611
00:42:14.566 --> 00:42:17.667
         - I was hungry.
      I was in the kitchen.

612
00:42:17.669 --> 00:42:20.503
- Well... now that you are here,

613
00:42:20.505 --> 00:42:24.374
    show me where your mother
       keeps her jewelry.

614
00:42:29.014 --> 00:42:30.647
        Goodbye, sister.

615
00:43:11.056 --> 00:43:12.855
          - It's okay.

616
00:43:12.857 --> 00:43:16.125
 Everything is gonna be alright,
              baby.

617
00:43:30.275 --> 00:43:32.075
       - Ramin, eat, yes.

618
00:43:32.077 --> 00:43:33.643
         (Ramin moaning)

619
00:43:33.645 --> 00:43:35.278
           It's okay.

620
00:43:35.280 --> 00:43:37.380
- They already killed my mother.

621
00:43:38.283 --> 00:43:40.516
  They really killed my mother.

622
00:43:49.294 --> 00:43:50.960
       (PA):<i> Bijan Yadgar.</i>

623
00:43:52.297 --> 00:43:54.364
         <i> Behrooz Ghodsi.</i>

624
00:43:55.900 --> 00:43:58.368
        <i> Jahanshah Soheil.</i>

625
00:44:00.105 --> 00:44:01.971
           <i> Isaac Amin.</i>

626
00:44:02.907 --> 00:44:04.674
         <i> Vartan Sofoyan.</i>

627
00:44:04.676 --> 00:44:07.110
     (soft, dramatic music)

628
00:44:07.112 --> 00:44:08.978
          <i> Ramin Ameri.</i>

629
00:44:14.085 --> 00:44:15.752
           (shouting)

630
00:44:17.422 --> 00:44:19.389
           (shouting)

631
00:44:22.527 --> 00:44:24.560
           (shouting)

632
00:44:28.667 --> 00:44:30.400
           (shouting)

633
00:44:32.504 --> 00:44:35.171
      - It will be alright.
   Isaac, it will be alright.

634
00:44:35.173 --> 00:44:36.839
          You will see.

635
00:44:36.841 --> 00:44:40.943
       Seventy-two virgins
 may be waiting for each of us.

636
00:44:40.945 --> 00:44:43.579
           (shouting)
        (man crying out)

637
00:44:46.785 --> 00:44:48.785
           (shouting)

638
00:44:52.390 --> 00:44:53.856
            - Isaac!

639
00:44:53.858 --> 00:44:56.125
          Isaac! Isaac!
             - Move!

640
00:44:56.127 --> 00:44:58.728
 - Isaac, please! Isaac, please!

641
00:44:58.730 --> 00:45:02.031
          (crying out)
           (shouting)

642
00:45:05.837 --> 00:45:07.804
        (dramatic music)

643
00:45:10.975 --> 00:45:13.042
            (gunfire)

644
00:45:14.479 --> 00:45:16.045
            (gunfire)

645
00:45:31.563 --> 00:45:34.097
    (guard shouting in Farsi)

646
00:45:36.568 --> 00:45:38.634
           (groaning)

647
00:45:46.377 --> 00:45:48.077
           (coughing)

648
00:45:50.415 --> 00:45:52.148
            (panting)

649
00:46:02.427 --> 00:46:04.293
         (distant cries)

650
00:46:06.030 --> 00:46:07.864
        (distant gunfire)

651
00:46:35.059 --> 00:46:38.461
- Your mother is feeling better?
     - Much better,<i> khanoum.</i>

652
00:46:38.463 --> 00:46:40.163
        - Hold on. Sugar.

653
00:46:40.165 --> 00:46:43.132
    - Thank you. Her birthday
     was a real celebration.

654
00:46:43.134 --> 00:46:44.967
    You should see my nephew,

655
00:46:44.969 --> 00:46:47.570
       what a handsome boy
         he's becoming.

656
00:46:47.572 --> 00:46:51.974
   In a few years, he'll make
   a fine husband for Shirin.

657
00:46:51.976 --> 00:46:54.177
  - And Morteza? Was he there?

658
00:46:54.179 --> 00:46:58.648
 - No,<i> khanoum,</i> he doesn't come
   to these family gatherings.

659
00:46:58.650 --> 00:47:01.284
            He thinks
   he has better things to do.

660
00:47:01.286 --> 00:47:02.919
         - Like looting.

661
00:47:07.659 --> 00:47:09.358
             - What?

662
00:47:12.864 --> 00:47:15.031
      - He didn't tell you.

663
00:47:15.033 --> 00:47:17.200
    He looted Isaac's office.

664
00:47:17.202 --> 00:47:19.101
   He and the other employees.

665
00:47:19.103 --> 00:47:20.870
          - My Morteza?

666
00:47:20.872 --> 00:47:24.307
    - I was there, I saw it.
      - You misunderstood.

667
00:47:24.309 --> 00:47:27.610
   - He said they were moving
    the goods somewhere else

668
00:47:27.612 --> 00:47:29.812
        for safekeeping,
       but I know better.

669
00:47:29.814 --> 00:47:32.114
       - You know better?

670
00:47:32.116 --> 00:47:35.618
   What is it that you see it
          always right?

671
00:47:35.620 --> 00:47:39.555
Is it possible you choose to see
         what you want?

672
00:47:39.557 --> 00:47:42.558
       - I saw what I saw.
     - You saw what you saw.

673
00:47:42.560 --> 00:47:44.694
      You're a kind woman,
         Farnaz-khanoum,

674
00:47:44.696 --> 00:47:46.896
    but you're full of scorn.

675
00:47:46.898 --> 00:47:49.332
  When I tell you maybe one day

676
00:47:49.334 --> 00:47:51.701
   my little nephew will marry
          your Shirin,

677
00:47:51.703 --> 00:47:53.836
    do you think I'm serious?

678
00:47:53.838 --> 00:47:56.405
  I say these things as a joke.

679
00:47:56.407 --> 00:47:59.742
  I know you will never tell me
      how you really feel,

680
00:47:59.744 --> 00:48:01.911
so you say nothing or you smile!

681
00:48:01.913 --> 00:48:04.480
 - I am telling you what I saw.

682
00:48:04.482 --> 00:48:09.051
         I saw your son
     and the other employees

683
00:48:09.053 --> 00:48:11.921
    taking jewels, paintings,
         tables, chairs!

684
00:48:11.923 --> 00:48:13.689
   And when I confronted him,

685
00:48:13.691 --> 00:48:16.192
  he said that Isaac had to pay

686
00:48:16.194 --> 00:48:19.428
          for the sins
  of a whole collection of men.

687
00:48:19.430 --> 00:48:22.064
         - He said this?
             - Yes.

688
00:48:22.066 --> 00:48:25.334
     - Well, maybe Amin-agha
           should pay.

689
00:48:25.336 --> 00:48:28.571
  Maybe it's time someone paid.

690
00:48:28.573 --> 00:48:30.940
        - Isaac has never
         harmed anybody,

691
00:48:30.942 --> 00:48:34.343
 least of all you and your son.

692
00:48:34.345 --> 00:48:36.178
    He does not have to pay.

693
00:48:36.180 --> 00:48:38.014
  - Why is it that some people

694
00:48:38.016 --> 00:48:40.783
     were meant to be served
        on hand and foot,

695
00:48:40.785 --> 00:48:43.619
  and all others could hope for
      was washing toilets?

696
00:48:43.621 --> 00:48:45.688
        - You think Isaac
       was born a prince?

697
00:48:45.690 --> 00:48:49.191
     No, Habibeh, the money
    didn't fall from the sky.

698
00:48:49.193 --> 00:48:51.360
   You work hard, you do well.

699
00:48:51.362 --> 00:48:53.963
         - I work hard.
       My son works hard.

700
00:48:53.965 --> 00:48:57.967
 - And you have come a long way
     from where you started.

701
00:48:57.969 --> 00:48:59.769
     Do I need to remind you

702
00:48:59.771 --> 00:49:02.972
      of the way you lived
        when we met you,

703
00:49:02.974 --> 00:49:05.107
   you and your snot-nosed son

704
00:49:05.109 --> 00:49:07.610
         selling flowers
      on a street corner?!

705
00:49:07.612 --> 00:49:10.546
      You were so emaciated
        that you fainted!

706
00:49:10.548 --> 00:49:15.084
      We got out of the car
      and Isaac said to me:

707
00:49:15.086 --> 00:49:19.689
"Isn't there something we can do
     to help these people?"

708
00:49:21.993 --> 00:49:24.527
       And we took you in.

709
00:49:26.631 --> 00:49:28.798
       Now, you tell me...

710
00:49:28.800 --> 00:49:32.668
     is this what my husband
         has to pay for?

711
00:50:00.031 --> 00:50:03.733
      - You say you wanted
        to become a poet.

712
00:50:06.838 --> 00:50:08.738
        So write me this.

713
00:50:09.674 --> 00:50:11.474
       How does a poet...

714
00:50:11.476 --> 00:50:14.110
     become such a rich man?

715
00:50:23.888 --> 00:50:26.489
    - Perhaps because the...

716
00:50:26.491 --> 00:50:30.059
  the jeweller... and the poet

717
00:50:30.061 --> 00:50:32.128
    share the same weakness.

718
00:50:33.498 --> 00:50:35.231
       We seek perfection.

719
00:50:35.233 --> 00:50:40.136
      - There is no mention
of any friends or acquaintances.

720
00:50:40.138 --> 00:50:43.472
  - I'm an introvert by nature,
            brother.

721
00:50:43.474 --> 00:50:47.309
   I... I enjoy spending time
         with my family

722
00:50:47.311 --> 00:50:50.312
       or... being alone.

723
00:50:50.314 --> 00:50:53.549
    - Then we've brought you
       to the right place.

724
00:51:03.094 --> 00:51:05.161
    (whipping and screaming)

725
00:51:07.098 --> 00:51:08.964
           Hear that?

726
00:51:09.534 --> 00:51:11.600
    (whipping and screaming)

727
00:51:19.744 --> 00:51:21.410
            Now talk.

728
00:51:28.553 --> 00:51:30.786
      - What do you want me
          to tell you?

729
00:51:30.788 --> 00:51:34.757
 I... I don't know the answers,
    I don't know what to sa--

730
00:51:34.759 --> 00:51:37.993
 - Tell me about your activities
         for the Shah!!

731
00:51:40.531 --> 00:51:43.265
   And that brother of yours!

732
00:51:43.267 --> 00:51:44.934
          Where is he?!

733
00:51:44.936 --> 00:51:46.936
     - I swear I don't know.

734
00:51:46.938 --> 00:51:48.938
           I swear...

735
00:51:48.940 --> 00:51:51.574
        Brother, I swear.

736
00:51:51.576 --> 00:51:53.375
            Brother--

737
00:51:53.377 --> 00:51:56.946
       - Brother Mustafa,
 your next man is ready for you.

738
00:51:56.948 --> 00:51:58.981
       - Brother, please.

739
00:51:58.983 --> 00:52:02.985
        I swear, brother,
  I swear to you, I don't know.

740
00:52:02.987 --> 00:52:05.855
    Please, brother, please.

741
00:52:20.738 --> 00:52:22.805
     (soft, dramatic music)

742
00:52:22.807 --> 00:52:24.874
             (blow)
          (exclaiming)

743
00:53:12.190 --> 00:53:14.290
        (dramatic music)

744
00:53:15.860 --> 00:53:18.093
  (indistinct PA announcement)

745
00:53:28.873 --> 00:53:30.306
          - Psst-psst.

746
00:53:32.043 --> 00:53:34.210
     - Navid, you scared me.

747
00:53:34.212 --> 00:53:36.645
  Did you find out where he is?

748
00:53:36.647 --> 00:53:39.448
- I wish I had more information.

749
00:53:41.085 --> 00:53:43.018
     The friend who told me
      about Isaac's arrest

750
00:53:43.020 --> 00:53:44.987
    tells me that the Guards
       are after me, too.

751
00:53:44.989 --> 00:53:47.656
     - They will get us all
           at the end.

752
00:53:47.658 --> 00:53:51.260
   - Next month I'm expecting
lots of cash from a transaction.

753
00:53:51.262 --> 00:53:54.230
       I will use the cash
      to pay the smugglers.

754
00:53:54.232 --> 00:53:56.599
        They will take me
       over the mountains.

755
00:53:56.601 --> 00:53:58.734
       - What transaction?

756
00:53:58.736 --> 00:54:01.070
      - I'm importing vodka
          from Russia.

757
00:54:01.072 --> 00:54:03.105
     - If they catch you...

758
00:54:03.107 --> 00:54:05.174
     they will execute you.

759
00:54:05.176 --> 00:54:08.210
 - I can't really talk about it.
 The less you know, the better.

760
00:54:08.212 --> 00:54:10.546
       The only thing is,
      I need a bit of cash

761
00:54:10.548 --> 00:54:12.448
         to hold me over
   until the shipment arrives.

762
00:54:12.450 --> 00:54:15.684
     - How much do you need?
         - About 10,000.

763
00:54:15.686 --> 00:54:17.519
           - Dollars?

764
00:54:17.521 --> 00:54:20.589
          - Of course.
    - That's a lot of money.

765
00:54:20.591 --> 00:54:23.392
           - Please...
  if I don't get out of Tehran,

766
00:54:23.394 --> 00:54:25.327
   they're bound to catch me.

767
00:54:28.532 --> 00:54:30.266
       - On one condition.

768
00:54:30.268 --> 00:54:34.236
       If anything happens
        to Isaac and I...

769
00:54:34.238 --> 00:54:36.105
       you will see to it

770
00:54:36.107 --> 00:54:40.376
     that Shirin and Parviz
     are safe and together.

771
00:54:42.546 --> 00:54:44.313
           Promise me.

772
00:54:44.315 --> 00:54:46.181
          - I promise.

773
00:54:48.586 --> 00:54:50.452
  (indistinct PA announcement)

774
00:55:02.566 --> 00:55:05.200
            (sighing)
   - You can fill in the rest.

775
00:55:06.771 --> 00:55:08.637
        - One more thing.

776
00:55:14.345 --> 00:55:16.679
            (gasping)

777
00:55:18.149 --> 00:55:20.215
            - My God.

778
00:55:22.987 --> 00:55:24.586
            My ring.

779
00:55:24.588 --> 00:55:26.822
      - I needed collateral
    against the money I owed.

780
00:55:26.824 --> 00:55:30.225
   I didn't mention it because
    I knew I would return it.

781
00:55:31.796 --> 00:55:33.329
        So long, Farnaz.

782
00:55:33.331 --> 00:55:35.998
    Kiss little Shirin for me
        and, God willing,

783
00:55:36.000 --> 00:55:38.667
         I will see you
    on some other continent.

784
00:55:38.669 --> 00:55:41.704
   Please, you need to leave,
            as well.

785
00:55:47.978 --> 00:55:49.678
         (gate clanging)

786
00:55:54.819 --> 00:55:56.452
           (coughing)

787
00:56:00.458 --> 00:56:02.091
            - Water.

788
00:56:12.370 --> 00:56:14.703
         Fresh bandages.

789
00:56:15.840 --> 00:56:18.107
          - Thank you.

790
00:56:24.215 --> 00:56:26.014
        - Have you cried?

791
00:56:26.016 --> 00:56:28.417
       - I can't anymore.

792
00:56:28.419 --> 00:56:30.219
           (sniffling)

793
00:56:30.221 --> 00:56:32.721
- You'll feel better if you cry.

794
00:56:36.427 --> 00:56:38.293
           (shrieking)

795
00:56:41.665 --> 00:56:44.500
       (running footfalls)
      Mohsen's little boy.

796
00:56:46.670 --> 00:56:51.106
 - Why would he bring his child
      to a place like this?

797
00:56:51.108 --> 00:56:54.009
     - Mohsen is very proud
           of his son.

798
00:56:54.011 --> 00:56:55.677
            You know?

799
00:56:55.679 --> 00:56:58.680
   He himself was in the same
     prison for many years,

800
00:56:58.682 --> 00:57:01.350
       tortured by Savak.

801
00:57:01.352 --> 00:57:04.086
       - Do you know why?

802
00:57:04.088 --> 00:57:06.155
  - They didn't need a reason.

803
00:57:09.894 --> 00:57:12.161
   - So the missing finger...

804
00:57:13.898 --> 00:57:16.432
  - That's not the only torture
          he underwent.

805
00:57:16.434 --> 00:57:20.235
 Let's just say he never thought
     he could have a child.

806
00:57:20.237 --> 00:57:23.772
  That little boy is a miracle,
      a badge of his faith.

807
00:57:24.708 --> 00:57:26.542
       He's not a bad man.

808
00:57:28.946 --> 00:57:32.347
      You may have trouble
  believing that, but he's not.

809
00:57:45.296 --> 00:57:47.196
          - The Koran?

810
00:57:48.499 --> 00:57:50.566
    - Have you ever read it?

811
00:57:52.736 --> 00:57:55.304
   You might find it helpful.

812
00:57:55.306 --> 00:57:58.307
       You have to believe
     that you will make it.

813
00:57:58.309 --> 00:58:00.209
           Have faith.

814
00:58:38.182 --> 00:58:40.048
         (phone ringing)

815
00:58:41.352 --> 00:58:43.018
            - Hello?

816
00:58:43.020 --> 00:58:44.620
             - Mama!

817
00:58:44.622 --> 00:58:47.789
   - Sweetheart, how are you?

818
00:58:47.791 --> 00:58:49.558
          -<i> I'm great.</i>

819
00:58:49.560 --> 00:58:52.561
   <i> Actually, I'm just about to</i>
 <i> play baseball with my friends,</i>

820
00:58:52.563 --> 00:58:54.696
  <i> but, uh, I was wanting to...</i>

821
00:58:54.698 --> 00:58:57.165
         <i> I was wondering</i>
       <i> if Baba was there.</i>

822
00:58:57.167 --> 00:59:00.068
 <i> I wanted to say happy birthday</i>
             <i> to him.</i>

823
00:59:02.573 --> 00:59:05.207
  - I'm afraid he is not here.

824
00:59:05.209 --> 00:59:07.609
       - What do you mean?
Must be close to midnight there.

825
00:59:08.579 --> 00:59:10.212
              <i> Mama?</i>

826
00:59:10.214 --> 00:59:12.748
     Mama, what's going on?

827
00:59:15.319 --> 00:59:18.120
     Mama, wh-where is Baba?

828
00:59:20.224 --> 00:59:22.291
      - He's been arrested.

829
00:59:23.027 --> 00:59:24.860
             - What?

830
00:59:24.862 --> 00:59:26.328
       - I went to prison,

831
00:59:26.330 --> 00:59:28.931
    but they wouldn't tell me
            anything.

832
00:59:28.933 --> 00:59:32.301
         - Is he alive?
         - I don't know.

833
00:59:33.404 --> 00:59:35.304
          I'm so sorry.

834
00:59:38.409 --> 00:59:40.909
 We should've left when you did.

835
00:59:40.911 --> 00:59:43.879
          - It's okay.
         - No, it's not.

836
00:59:43.881 --> 00:59:45.614
  -<i> Please, please, Mama, shhh.</i>

837
00:59:45.616 --> 00:59:47.616
        <i> It's okay, Mama.</i>

838
00:59:47.618 --> 00:59:49.484
         - I'm so sorry.

839
00:59:52.856 --> 00:59:56.258
   I just loved we were here.

840
00:59:56.260 --> 00:59:57.893
    - Okay, I'm coming home.

841
00:59:57.895 --> 00:59:59.928
        - Nah, nah, nah--
         -<i> Mama, please!</i>

842
00:59:59.930 --> 01:00:03.265
      - You stay in school,
        for you're safe.

843
01:00:03.267 --> 01:00:05.434
<i>There's nothing you can do here.</i>

844
01:00:05.436 --> 01:00:07.803
    There's nothing I can do.

845
01:00:07.805 --> 01:00:10.639
      They will release him
        when they realize

846
01:00:10.641 --> 01:00:12.374
  <i> that he's done nothing wrong.</i>

847
01:00:12.376 --> 01:00:13.942
      And we will get out.

848
01:00:16.280 --> 01:00:20.549
        Please promise me
  that you will not come back,

849
01:00:20.551 --> 01:00:22.985
    that you will stay there.

850
01:00:24.922 --> 01:00:28.223
  - Okay, okay, I... I promise.

851
01:00:28.225 --> 01:00:32.260
 - I need to leave the line open
 in case your uncle calls, okay?

852
01:00:32.262 --> 01:00:34.830
  - And what about Shirin, huh?

853
01:00:34.832 --> 01:00:37.366
   - She's upstairs... asleep.

854
01:00:38.302 --> 01:00:40.235
          We are okay.

855
01:00:41.905 --> 01:00:44.172
   We will see you very soon.

856
01:00:50.481 --> 01:00:52.848
     We love you very much.

857
01:00:52.850 --> 01:00:54.750
       - I love you, too.

858
01:01:18.509 --> 01:01:20.575
        (groaning softly)

859
01:01:26.717 --> 01:01:28.583
         (gate clanging)

860
01:01:30.354 --> 01:01:32.020
           (shouting)

861
01:01:33.290 --> 01:01:35.357
     (groaning and grunting)

862
01:01:39.730 --> 01:01:41.363
           (groaning)

863
01:01:41.365 --> 01:01:42.964
           (shouting)

864
01:01:42.966 --> 01:01:45.367
           (groaning)

865
01:01:45.369 --> 01:01:47.536
           (shouting)

866
01:01:47.538 --> 01:01:50.706
           (groaning)
    (guard shouting in Farsi)

867
01:01:52.976 --> 01:01:55.043
             (Farsi)
           (groaning)

868
01:01:56.980 --> 01:01:58.747
       (shouting in Farsi)

869
01:01:58.749 --> 01:02:00.515
       (Isaac whimpering)

870
01:02:00.517 --> 01:02:02.451
       (shouting in Farsi)

871
01:02:05.989 --> 01:02:07.923
        (rifles cocking)

872
01:02:14.765 --> 01:02:16.631
            (gunfire)

873
01:02:28.011 --> 01:02:29.644
              - Ah!

874
01:02:34.585 --> 01:02:37.085
            (gunfire)
          (whimpering)

875
01:02:39.623 --> 01:02:41.857
            (gunfire)

876
01:02:46.230 --> 01:02:47.863
          (crying out)

877
01:02:59.042 --> 01:03:00.976
          (whimpering)

878
01:03:02.613 --> 01:03:04.513
            (crying)

879
01:03:11.255 --> 01:03:12.888
            (sobbing)

880
01:03:30.007 --> 01:03:31.907
            (sobbing)

881
01:03:42.085 --> 01:03:43.919
         (Muslim prayer)

882
01:03:50.794 --> 01:03:53.628
       - What can you say
        in your defence?

883
01:03:53.630 --> 01:03:55.964
      - What I said before.

884
01:03:55.966 --> 01:03:58.300
       That I'm innocent.

885
01:03:58.302 --> 01:03:59.935
           (sniffling)

886
01:04:03.874 --> 01:04:06.575
      I will also say this.

887
01:04:08.111 --> 01:04:10.312
              I...

888
01:04:10.314 --> 01:04:13.582
         I have followed
     the wrong path in life.

889
01:04:15.519 --> 01:04:18.420
  I pursued material wealth...

890
01:04:19.690 --> 01:04:23.124
      ...which in the end,
       brought me nothing.

891
01:04:23.126 --> 01:04:25.126
           - Nothing?

892
01:04:25.128 --> 01:04:26.795
      Look at your villas,

893
01:04:26.797 --> 01:04:30.532
       the trips you took,
       the cars you drove.

894
01:04:30.534 --> 01:04:33.401
       Me, I have nothing.

895
01:04:34.638 --> 01:04:37.372
        For two years,
   my son wore the same shoes,

896
01:04:37.374 --> 01:04:40.208
   because I couldn't buy him
           a new pair.

897
01:04:40.210 --> 01:04:43.078
           In the end,
     I had to cut the front

898
01:04:43.080 --> 01:04:45.413
     so his feet could grow.

899
01:04:46.350 --> 01:04:48.550
          - Yes, but...

900
01:04:48.552 --> 01:04:50.619
         look at me now.

901
01:04:51.555 --> 01:04:53.421
        And look at you.

902
01:04:55.726 --> 01:04:58.326
    I sit here before you...

903
01:04:58.328 --> 01:05:00.929
     my fate in your hands.

904
01:05:00.931 --> 01:05:02.998
        (Mohsen scoffing)

905
01:05:06.370 --> 01:05:08.169
         My daughter...

906
01:05:08.171 --> 01:05:11.740
with her closet full of shoes...

907
01:05:11.742 --> 01:05:14.509
has no idea where her father is.

908
01:05:14.511 --> 01:05:18.280
     The power of Abu Lahab
         will perish...

909
01:05:18.282 --> 01:05:20.248
       and he will perish.

910
01:05:20.918 --> 01:05:24.886
    His wealth and his gains
      will not exempt him.

911
01:05:24.888 --> 01:05:27.756
   - Very well said, brother.

912
01:05:27.758 --> 01:05:31.126
     I see you've been using
        your time wisely.

913
01:05:31.128 --> 01:05:34.596
         I did the same
      when I was in prison.

914
01:05:34.598 --> 01:05:36.264
             I read.

915
01:05:37.200 --> 01:05:39.834
   They were difficult years,
             but...

916
01:05:41.972 --> 01:05:43.772
          ...the Koran,

917
01:05:43.774 --> 01:05:46.207
     the Koran gave me hope.

918
01:05:46.209 --> 01:05:49.945
  You know that I bring my son
         here every day?

919
01:05:49.947 --> 01:05:54.149
 - That is what I hear going up
     and down above my cell?

920
01:05:54.151 --> 01:05:58.486
  - I once sat in a chair very
  similar to the one you're in.

921
01:06:00.424 --> 01:06:03.325
Now that the tables have turned,

922
01:06:03.327 --> 01:06:06.761
 why should I have mercy on you?

923
01:06:06.763 --> 01:06:08.596
 - Because I have nothing to do

924
01:06:08.598 --> 01:06:10.765
         with the people
      who caused you pain.

925
01:06:10.767 --> 01:06:13.068
        - Oh, but you do.

926
01:06:13.070 --> 01:06:15.971
     You look the other way.

927
01:06:15.973 --> 01:06:18.840
 - Yes, you're right about that.

928
01:06:18.842 --> 01:06:20.809
        I... I was blind.

929
01:06:20.811 --> 01:06:23.311
      I recognize that now.

930
01:06:24.648 --> 01:06:26.881
     But, please, brother...

931
01:06:28.452 --> 01:06:33.621
   ...if you say that you sat
    in the same chair as me,

932
01:06:33.623 --> 01:06:36.257
   then you must know my fear.

933
01:06:36.259 --> 01:06:38.259
       And more than that,

934
01:06:38.261 --> 01:06:40.362
       my... despair at...

935
01:06:40.364 --> 01:06:43.999
  never seeing my family again.

936
01:06:44.001 --> 01:06:47.902
  - I not only know your fear,
         I can smell it.

937
01:06:49.673 --> 01:06:52.007
   Afraid I've gotten addicted
             to it.

938
01:06:52.009 --> 01:06:54.042
        - Than you are...

939
01:06:54.044 --> 01:06:57.746
    as much a prisoner today
            as I am.

940
01:07:03.053 --> 01:07:07.122
   Your mercy may liberate me
       from these walls...

941
01:07:08.058 --> 01:07:10.358
    ...but more than that...

942
01:07:12.295 --> 01:07:14.929
       ...it will save you
         from yourself.

943
01:07:34.718 --> 01:07:37.152
      I can change my ways.

944
01:07:42.325 --> 01:07:44.893
    I can prove my sincerity.

945
01:07:44.895 --> 01:07:47.095
        Perhaps I can...

946
01:07:47.097 --> 01:07:50.198
        sustain the cause
        of the revolution

947
01:07:50.200 --> 01:07:52.333
    with a generous donation.

948
01:07:52.335 --> 01:07:54.402
         - How generous?

949
01:07:55.872 --> 01:07:57.705
   - As generous as necessary.

950
01:07:57.707 --> 01:08:00.909
 - I've received similar offers
        before, brother.

951
01:08:00.911 --> 01:08:03.411
     None was satisfactory.

952
01:08:05.749 --> 01:08:08.983
 I need a more specific answer.

953
01:08:10.554 --> 01:08:12.187
          - Everything.

954
01:08:14.758 --> 01:08:17.192
     My entire life savings.

955
01:08:20.130 --> 01:08:21.996
           Everything.

956
01:08:34.945 --> 01:08:37.011
     (soft, dramatic music)

957
01:08:51.795 --> 01:08:53.795
    I have to go home first.

958
01:08:53.797 --> 01:08:56.798
    The bank will need proof
       of identification.

959
01:08:56.800 --> 01:08:59.400
        - You don't have
     your driver's license?

960
01:08:59.402 --> 01:09:02.036
 - My wallet was never returned
         to me, brother.

961
01:09:05.442 --> 01:09:07.509
           (groaning)

962
01:09:39.643 --> 01:09:41.709
        (sharp knocking)

963
01:09:42.846 --> 01:09:44.913
            (banging)

964
01:10:02.032 --> 01:10:03.731
            - Isaac.

965
01:10:05.569 --> 01:10:07.335
   - We don't have much time,
             sister.

966
01:10:07.337 --> 01:10:09.837
   - My passport, where is it?

967
01:10:09.839 --> 01:10:11.906
         - The passports
        were confiscated.

968
01:10:11.908 --> 01:10:15.043
     They came through here
          like thieves.

969
01:10:15.045 --> 01:10:16.878
        They took it all.

970
01:10:16.880 --> 01:10:19.247
  - I need some identification
          for the bank!

971
01:10:19.249 --> 01:10:20.982
           (groaning)

972
01:10:20.984 --> 01:10:23.651
    You can't keep this place
    in order while I'm gone?

973
01:10:23.653 --> 01:10:25.253
            - Isaac,
 I have your birth certificate.

974
01:10:25.255 --> 01:10:28.723
 - I need photo identification!
       - There's nothing.

975
01:10:28.725 --> 01:10:31.059
           - Brother,
    I'm sorry for the delay.

976
01:10:31.061 --> 01:10:33.728
           I'm sorry,
   th-there must be something.

977
01:10:33.730 --> 01:10:36.497
   - Let's go. Back to prison.

978
01:10:36.499 --> 01:10:38.333
            - But...

979
01:10:38.335 --> 01:10:40.802
           - No, no...

980
01:10:41.905 --> 01:10:44.839
- Brother... Brother, please.
             - Now.

981
01:10:44.841 --> 01:10:47.075
         - They've taken
  all my photo identification.

982
01:10:47.077 --> 01:10:49.344
      My passport was taken
         by your guards

983
01:10:49.346 --> 01:10:51.279
   when they came to my house.

984
01:10:51.281 --> 01:10:53.948
   Please... please, brother,
      take me to the bank.

985
01:10:53.950 --> 01:10:56.084
      - And waste my time?!
             - Wait!

986
01:10:56.086 --> 01:10:58.620
  Wait! Please. Please, please!

987
01:10:58.622 --> 01:11:02.457
          They will...
      they'll recognize me.

988
01:11:02.459 --> 01:11:06.060
           They will.
I've been a client for 20 years.

989
01:11:06.062 --> 01:11:07.528
     They will recognize me.

990
01:11:07.530 --> 01:11:09.797
        Fariborz Jamshidi
         is the manager.

991
01:11:09.799 --> 01:11:12.800
         He was a teller
   when I opened the account.

992
01:11:19.576 --> 01:11:22.477
     - I can come with you.
   - Stay with Shirin. Shirin.

993
01:11:27.751 --> 01:11:29.817
        (dramatic music)

994
01:12:00.583 --> 01:12:02.583
  - He appears to be off today.

995
01:12:02.585 --> 01:12:05.353
              - No,
  I'm sure he's in the office.

996
01:12:05.355 --> 01:12:07.689
        - May I help you?

997
01:12:07.691 --> 01:12:09.223
           - Fariborz.

998
01:12:10.160 --> 01:12:12.093
         It's me, Isaac.

999
01:12:12.095 --> 01:12:14.762
            - Isaac?

1000
01:12:15.999 --> 01:12:18.800
     - I would like to close
    all of my accounts today.

1001
01:12:18.802 --> 01:12:20.335
          All in cash.

1002
01:12:21.171 --> 01:12:24.238
  - You heard the man, brother.
         Now get going.

1003
01:12:25.809 --> 01:12:28.242
      - Yes... right away.

1004
01:12:29.179 --> 01:12:30.878
           Follow me.

1005
01:12:38.722 --> 01:12:40.888
        (dramatic music)

1006
01:12:53.069 --> 01:12:54.469
              - So?

1007
01:12:59.309 --> 01:13:02.043
     - You're free, brother.

1008
01:13:02.045 --> 01:13:06.047
        My hands are tied
 if they come back to you again.

1009
01:13:06.049 --> 01:13:07.915
       And they will soon.

1010
01:14:37.507 --> 01:14:39.574
           (whistling)

1011
01:15:01.531 --> 01:15:04.565
    - Amin-agha! You're free?

1012
01:15:05.969 --> 01:15:08.703
 - Didn't your friends tell you?

1013
01:15:08.705 --> 01:15:11.038
     - Uh, it's been a while
      since I've seen them,

1014
01:15:11.040 --> 01:15:12.773
         but I was sure
     you would be released.

1015
01:15:12.775 --> 01:15:15.543
That's what I kept telling them,
     but you know how it is.

1016
01:15:15.545 --> 01:15:17.879
  - So what are you doing here
              now?

1017
01:15:17.881 --> 01:15:21.048
   - Now? Trying to figure out
   what's been taken from you.

1018
01:15:21.050 --> 01:15:23.985
       You know, I wanted
    to keep a record for you.

1019
01:15:23.987 --> 01:15:27.255
 - I am not a halfwit, Morteza.

1020
01:15:28.191 --> 01:15:30.558
  I know what took place here.

1021
01:15:30.560 --> 01:15:32.493
         You're a thief.

1022
01:15:32.495 --> 01:15:34.662
         - Me, a thief?

1023
01:15:34.664 --> 01:15:38.032
 - Show me this so-called record
         you're keeping.

1024
01:15:38.034 --> 01:15:40.801
  - I was just getting started.
  Let's start downstairs, okay?

1025
01:15:40.803 --> 01:15:43.804
       - I... I am tired.

1026
01:15:43.806 --> 01:15:48.209
    I don't have the strength
   or the taste for any games.

1027
01:15:48.211 --> 01:15:52.246
  Whatever you stole is yours,
       we both know that.

1028
01:15:52.248 --> 01:15:56.317
       There are no courts
       for me to turn to,

1029
01:15:56.319 --> 01:15:59.020
  but at least have the decency

1030
01:15:59.022 --> 01:16:00.988
     to look me in the face

1031
01:16:00.990 --> 01:16:02.823
    and tell me what you are.

1032
01:16:02.825 --> 01:16:06.327
      The only thing worse
 than a criminal is a hypocrite.

1033
01:16:15.238 --> 01:16:17.672
   - I wouldn't talk this way
         if I were you.

1034
01:16:20.843 --> 01:16:23.911
           You see...
 I have a document in my pocket

1035
01:16:23.913 --> 01:16:27.048
that could make a lot of trouble
            for you.

1036
01:16:27.050 --> 01:16:29.917
  - And what document is that?
             - Oh...

1037
01:16:29.919 --> 01:16:32.620
  the past has a way of coming
  back to haunt us, doesn't it?

1038
01:16:32.622 --> 01:16:34.922
        - What document?

1039
01:16:42.398 --> 01:16:44.599
        - Remember this?

1040
01:16:44.601 --> 01:16:47.335
          Remember? No?

1041
01:16:48.638 --> 01:16:51.505
           It's okay,
     I can read it for you.

1042
01:16:52.809 --> 01:16:57.445
"Sale of... one ruby and diamond
 pendant to the Empress and..."

1043
01:16:57.447 --> 01:17:01.649
  Want me to read the attached
     note from Her Majesty?

1044
01:17:01.651 --> 01:17:04.552
      "Thank you, Mr. Amin,
for this impeccable workmanship.

1045
01:17:04.554 --> 01:17:08.122
      Iran is proud to have
 an artisan such as yourself--"

1046
01:17:08.124 --> 01:17:12.493
 - This is from a long time ago.
   This doesn't mean anything.

1047
01:17:12.495 --> 01:17:15.396
       - This is what made
        your reputation.

1048
01:17:16.132 --> 01:17:18.633
     And then all the women
with cash in their pockets

1049
01:17:18.635 --> 01:17:20.401
 come running to you after that?
              Huh?

1050
01:17:20.403 --> 01:17:22.637
  Thinking: If he's good enough
         for the queen,

1051
01:17:22.639 --> 01:17:24.739
              ooh,
 he must be good enough for me.

1052
01:17:24.741 --> 01:17:26.907
    This letter is your link
         with the Shah.

1053
01:17:26.909 --> 01:17:29.910
        - Give it to me.
       (Morteza laughing)

1054
01:17:29.912 --> 01:17:31.679
         Give it to me.

1055
01:17:31.681 --> 01:17:33.981
      - This piece of paper
   is your death certificate.

1056
01:17:33.983 --> 01:17:36.017
  Why should I give it up, huh?

1057
01:17:36.019 --> 01:17:39.687
        Oh, you're lucky
    I didn't find it sooner.

1058
01:17:39.689 --> 01:17:42.323
       - You already have
       all of the jewels,

1059
01:17:42.325 --> 01:17:43.924
      and took everything.

1060
01:17:43.926 --> 01:17:45.826
            What else
    could you possibly want?

1061
01:17:45.828 --> 01:17:48.929
      - I want the diamond.
             - What?

1062
01:17:48.931 --> 01:17:51.465
   - The one you brought back
          from Antwerp.

1063
01:17:51.467 --> 01:17:52.700
          It's perfect.

1064
01:18:02.512 --> 01:18:05.579
      - What if I told you
          I donated it?

1065
01:18:07.150 --> 01:18:10.351
  To the Revolutionary Guards.

1066
01:18:10.353 --> 01:18:12.153
     - I don't believe you.

1067
01:18:12.155 --> 01:18:14.221
     - Do you have a choice?

1068
01:18:22.965 --> 01:18:25.533
   - You give me that diamond!
    - How could you do this?

1069
01:18:25.535 --> 01:18:28.202
   - You give me that diamond,
     or this piece of paper

1070
01:18:28.204 --> 01:18:30.671
   will be sent to the office
        of Imam Khomeini!

1071
01:18:30.673 --> 01:18:33.541
       - You listen to me,
        you little shit!!

1072
01:18:33.543 --> 01:18:35.710
          You snitch!!

1073
01:18:35.712 --> 01:18:40.381
      I am on better terms
with the office of Imam Khomeini

1074
01:18:40.383 --> 01:18:42.983
     than you will ever be!!

1075
01:18:42.985 --> 01:18:47.254
       After all, I am one
    of their biggest donors!!

1076
01:18:49.192 --> 01:18:51.826
Along with that perfect diamond,

1077
01:18:51.828 --> 01:18:55.563
        I have given them
        my life savings,

1078
01:18:55.565 --> 01:18:59.567
   so all it would take for me
     to get you into trouble

1079
01:18:59.569 --> 01:19:02.570
      would be a phone call
      informing them of all

1080
01:19:02.572 --> 01:19:07.007
 of the things I would've loved
  to have donated to the cause,

1081
01:19:07.009 --> 01:19:08.776
   if they had not been stolen

1082
01:19:08.778 --> 01:19:13.481
      by a small-time punk
         named Morteza!!

1083
01:19:15.585 --> 01:19:18.085
     Do you understand me?!

1084
01:19:19.589 --> 01:19:21.789
     Do you understand me?!

1085
01:19:21.791 --> 01:19:23.591
             - Yes!
             - Yes!

1086
01:19:23.593 --> 01:19:26.494
             - Yes.
   - They are my friends now.

1087
01:19:27.430 --> 01:19:29.230
             - Okay.

1088
01:19:29.232 --> 01:19:31.265
      - Now you be careful.

1089
01:19:31.267 --> 01:19:33.868
     You be careful and go!

1090
01:19:35.772 --> 01:19:37.972
      I fucking raised you!

1091
01:19:39.242 --> 01:19:41.108
         I can find you.

1092
01:19:59.629 --> 01:20:01.529
           (sniffling)

1093
01:20:05.067 --> 01:20:06.901
            (crying)

1094
01:20:42.939 --> 01:20:45.306
        (mournful music)

1095
01:20:45.308 --> 01:20:46.941
           - Baba-jan!

1096
01:20:49.545 --> 01:20:51.579
        Baba-jan is here!

1097
01:20:59.522 --> 01:21:01.088
            Baba-jan!

1098
01:21:02.024 --> 01:21:04.191
      I missed you so much!

1099
01:21:21.711 --> 01:21:23.978
     (Western playing on TV)

1100
01:21:33.923 --> 01:21:36.156
          - Mama-agha.
            - Salud.

1101
01:21:36.158 --> 01:21:38.425
         - Dinner ready?
             - Soon.

1102
01:21:40.730 --> 01:21:43.364
   - You shouldn't be watching
         junk like that.

1103
01:21:43.366 --> 01:21:45.432
    - You have your opinions
       and I respect them,

1104
01:21:45.434 --> 01:21:47.768
        but you don't get
         to come in here

1105
01:21:47.770 --> 01:21:49.603
      and tell your mother
          how to live.

1106
01:21:49.605 --> 01:21:51.338
           - I don't?

1107
01:21:51.340 --> 01:21:53.607
        - No, you don't.

1108
01:21:58.748 --> 01:22:00.848
      - I do if I want to.

1109
01:22:00.850 --> 01:22:05.819
 - Don't you dare to stand there
 and threaten me like some thug!

1110
01:22:06.956 --> 01:22:10.424
    If you want to report me,
        then just do it!

1111
01:22:15.598 --> 01:22:17.197
          What is that?

1112
01:22:17.199 --> 01:22:19.199
          - A letter...

1113
01:22:19.201 --> 01:22:21.602
   written from the Shah to...

1114
01:22:21.604 --> 01:22:23.637
            Mr. Amin.

1115
01:22:23.639 --> 01:22:26.774
        - Don't you think
    he's been through enough?

1116
01:22:26.776 --> 01:22:29.310
        - Don't you think
   we've been through enough?

1117
01:22:29.312 --> 01:22:31.779
     - Give me that letter!
         - All that oil,

1118
01:22:31.781 --> 01:22:34.848
        going to everyone
        but us Iranians!

1119
01:22:37.420 --> 01:22:38.786
           - Morteza--

1120
01:22:38.788 --> 01:22:40.621
            - Mama...

1121
01:22:40.623 --> 01:22:43.524
    I-I'm doing this for you.

1122
01:22:44.427 --> 01:22:46.860
  - Then I'm asking you not to.

1123
01:22:47.797 --> 01:22:50.230
         - It's because
      you've been so cowed,

1124
01:22:50.232 --> 01:22:53.901
       you don't even know
 how to fight for what is yours!

1125
01:22:53.903 --> 01:22:56.003
         - Who are you?

1126
01:22:57.239 --> 01:22:59.773
 I don't recognize you anymore.

1127
01:22:59.775 --> 01:23:02.509
  You're a stranger in my home.

1128
01:23:03.446 --> 01:23:05.379
      I want you to leave.

1129
01:23:07.416 --> 01:23:09.516
          Now, Morteza.

1130
01:23:11.020 --> 01:23:14.855
   I want you to leave now...
       before I kill you!

1131
01:23:14.857 --> 01:23:16.623
       Before I kill you!
            - Mother!

1132
01:23:16.625 --> 01:23:17.858
      - Before I kill you!
         - Mother! Mama!

1133
01:23:17.860 --> 01:23:20.094
      - Before I kill you!
            - Mother!

1134
01:23:20.096 --> 01:23:22.463
        Okay! Okay! Okay!

1135
01:23:22.465 --> 01:23:23.964
             - Out!

1136
01:23:23.966 --> 01:23:25.833
             - Okay!

1137
01:23:25.835 --> 01:23:27.901
            (sobbing)

1138
01:23:40.049 --> 01:23:44.184
    - Boss, in our business,
    nothing can be predicted.

1139
01:23:44.186 --> 01:23:45.853
        Not the weather,

1140
01:23:45.855 --> 01:23:47.888
         not the Guards
    that patrol the borders,

1141
01:23:47.890 --> 01:23:50.391
       not the encounters
      with snakes or wars.

1142
01:23:50.393 --> 01:23:54.695
 You will need God by your side
   throughout this adventure.

1143
01:23:54.697 --> 01:23:58.665
 - I've called on God many times
       already this year.

1144
01:23:58.667 --> 01:24:02.069
     - Well, bring God along
  if he makes you feel better,

1145
01:24:02.071 --> 01:24:04.571
   but you have to pay a fare.

1146
01:24:13.315 --> 01:24:15.382
  - You can have them checked.

1147
01:24:17.319 --> 01:24:20.788
     Together they are worth
         about 150,000.

1148
01:24:26.729 --> 01:24:28.228
             - Yeah.

1149
01:24:29.331 --> 01:24:32.232
       - Can we leave now?
       - Tomorrow at dawn.

1150
01:24:32.234 --> 01:24:34.768
    Eat a good meal. Rest up.

1151
01:24:34.770 --> 01:24:37.638
      You're going to need
          your energy.

1152
01:25:36.966 --> 01:25:41.602
- Stop eating. You have to wait.
    What are you looking for?

1153
01:25:41.604 --> 01:25:43.170
     - Do we have any wine?

1154
01:25:43.172 --> 01:25:45.906
     - It is from Passover.

1155
01:25:46.809 --> 01:25:48.342
         - That will do.

1156
01:25:51.413 --> 01:25:53.247
            (banging)

1157
01:25:59.622 --> 01:26:01.255
            (banging)

1158
01:26:07.196 --> 01:26:08.896
            (banging)

1159
01:26:12.201 --> 01:26:14.434
     - I should have waited.

1160
01:26:14.436 --> 01:26:17.804
  Maybe if he'd fallen asleep,
  I could've taken the letter.

1161
01:26:17.806 --> 01:26:20.040
         I am so sorry.

1162
01:26:20.042 --> 01:26:23.510
 - Habibeh, it's not your fault.

1163
01:26:24.446 --> 01:26:28.448
- Did he say where he was going?
              - No.

1164
01:26:28.450 --> 01:26:30.350
      - Doesn't matter now.

1165
01:26:30.352 --> 01:26:32.286
     We're leaving tomorrow.

1166
01:26:35.457 --> 01:26:38.292
    We were just going to sit
           for dinner.

1167
01:26:39.228 --> 01:26:41.528
     Why don't you join us?

1168
01:26:47.670 --> 01:26:49.203
            - Please?

1169
01:27:08.490 --> 01:27:10.557
           -<i> L'chaim.</i>

1170
01:27:10.559 --> 01:27:12.659
           -<i> Salamati.</i>

1171
01:27:20.502 --> 01:27:23.070
           (laughter)
            - Please.

1172
01:27:23.072 --> 01:27:26.073
 - They're not as good as yours.

1173
01:27:32.181 --> 01:27:36.083
  - The whole time I was there,
        I thought of you.

1174
01:27:36.085 --> 01:27:38.518
           And Parviz.

1175
01:27:38.520 --> 01:27:40.354
          Your mother.

1176
01:27:42.725 --> 01:27:44.791
        I talked to you.

1177
01:27:45.928 --> 01:27:47.794
         I embraced you.

1178
01:27:49.732 --> 01:27:51.598
        I lived with you.

1179
01:27:58.307 --> 01:28:02.943
  I'm going to a desert island
    and I can only bring one.

1180
01:28:08.117 --> 01:28:09.816
             Parvez.

1181
01:28:12.121 --> 01:28:15.656
       I was reading this
         the day we met.

1182
01:28:15.658 --> 01:28:17.858
            - I know.

1183
01:28:22.064 --> 01:28:25.966
    - I saw Vartan Sofoyan...

1184
01:28:25.968 --> 01:28:27.634
           in prison.

1185
01:28:27.636 --> 01:28:30.037
          - So did I...

1186
01:28:31.340 --> 01:28:33.974
 ...when I went to look for you.

1187
01:28:33.976 --> 01:28:35.642
        - We were there.

1188
01:28:40.582 --> 01:28:43.150
 We ended up in the same block.

1189
01:28:43.152 --> 01:28:45.419
       I got to know him.

1190
01:28:47.589 --> 01:28:49.423
        They killed him.

1191
01:28:54.163 --> 01:28:56.430
        - I am so sorry.

1192
01:29:10.379 --> 01:29:12.245
           - Me, too.

1193
01:29:48.217 --> 01:29:50.717
         - This is what
     we've been looking for.

1194
01:29:51.653 --> 01:29:54.054
       He escaped custody
         just yesterday.

1195
01:29:54.056 --> 01:29:55.756
           - Yes, sir.

1196
01:29:55.758 --> 01:29:58.425
I was in the old office building
        when he came back

1197
01:29:58.427 --> 01:30:00.394
      looking for diamonds
       he kept in a safe.

1198
01:30:00.396 --> 01:30:03.130
My guess is that he was planning
      to leave the country.

1199
01:30:05.667 --> 01:30:09.169
     - I'll pass this along
   to the proper authorities.

1200
01:30:09.671 --> 01:30:13.840
 So tell me, where are the rest
        of the jewels?

1201
01:30:14.877 --> 01:30:16.810
  You're under arrest, brother.

1202
01:30:53.282 --> 01:30:55.549
    - This is for good luck.

1203
01:31:09.131 --> 01:31:12.499
        - This is the key
     to Isaac's desk drawer.

1204
01:31:12.501 --> 01:31:16.369
    It is where you will find
     the deed to the house.

1205
01:31:21.510 --> 01:31:23.410
         It's yours now.

1206
01:31:32.321 --> 01:31:34.221
           (sniffling)
              - Go.

1207
01:31:41.597 --> 01:31:43.830
     (soft, dramatic music)

1208
01:31:56.345 --> 01:31:58.778
            (gasping)
       - Close your eyes.

1209
01:32:02.117 --> 01:32:04.117
        (dramatic music)

1210
01:32:10.025 --> 01:32:11.625
           (laughter)

1211
01:32:19.201 --> 01:32:20.800
           (laughter)

1212
01:32:20.802 --> 01:32:22.569
             - Yes?

1213
01:32:22.571 --> 01:32:25.005
           (laughter)

1214
01:32:25.007 --> 01:32:27.207
            Yes, yes!

1215
01:32:27.209 --> 01:32:28.642
               Oh.

1216
01:32:36.818 --> 01:32:38.585
        (child laughing)

1217
01:32:38.587 --> 01:32:40.654
      - This just came in.

1218
01:33:00.275 --> 01:33:01.908
            - Farnaz.

1219
01:33:05.414 --> 01:33:07.247
   (Farnaz): They've seen us.

1220
01:33:12.087 --> 01:33:13.520
             - Shit.

1221
01:33:15.057 --> 01:33:16.923
            Hang on.

1222
01:33:18.694 --> 01:33:20.527
        (guards shouting)
          - Go, go, go!

1223
01:33:23.065 --> 01:33:24.497
   - They're coming after us.

1224
01:33:27.736 --> 01:33:30.470
  - Shirin, get down. Get down!

1225
01:33:40.649 --> 01:33:43.316
            (honking)

1226
01:34:03.739 --> 01:34:06.573
  I'm not going back to prison.

1227
01:34:07.342 --> 01:34:08.708
            Hang on.

1228
01:34:15.817 --> 01:34:18.151
             Shirin?

1229
01:34:18.153 --> 01:34:19.786
        - Just stay down.

1230
01:34:19.788 --> 01:34:22.355
           Stay down.

1231
01:34:38.707 --> 01:34:40.573
           - Okay, go.

1232
01:34:52.054 --> 01:34:54.788
       Around the corner.
             - Baba.

1233
01:35:28.390 --> 01:35:30.123
           - Come on.

1234
01:36:27.716 --> 01:36:29.549
    What was that all about?

1235
01:36:29.551 --> 01:36:31.718
       - They were asking
         for directions.

